/* NODUS // entries */
window.NODUS_REFS = {"c-vesper":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p2d946d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WOMAN ON THE ROOF</p><h2 class=\"pop-t h\">vesper</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horned</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>, and the first human being a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> returned as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">UNREADABLE</a>. Its reading of her came back UNINDEXED, with the line for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> blank, and the one thing it read from her was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-non-serviam\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-non-serviam\">NON SERVIAM</a>.</p><p>Her face is a ceramic <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casing</a>, its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> dim magenta at rest and white at full burn, and a plate on the side of the skull covers her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>. Her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> carry her signal on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, and cables run from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a> at the back of her skull down her spine. She is dry, patient and unsentimental, and she makes no speeches.</p><p>Her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a> is the evening star, which is the morning star seen from the other side of the night, since both are Venus. It is also the name of the evening prayer she would not kneel for as a girl, in a congregation of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> that refused <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. Her older sister was the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-watcher":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pd5b77f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AN ANGEL THAT READS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Watcher VII</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that reads, the seventh of the numbered <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watchers</a> over Nodus, made of three rings of thirteen eyes crossing like the hoops of an armillary, with nothing at its center. It held <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> from the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and read the souls there, and whatever could be seen from there, against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. It was the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> to return the verdict <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">UNREADABLE</a> on a human being.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-wheel":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p1ad3b6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">AN OPHAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Wheel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that came through the opening at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and took station nine hundred meters above the center of the city, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. It has three rings turning inside one another, their rims set with twenty-one, seventeen and thirteen eyes that open and close in shifts, a corona of thirty-two black blades, and one eye in the hub. It is the form Ezekiel gives the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ophan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">ophanim</a> (Ezekiel 1:16-18), and it is the largest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> anyone has seen. It held that station for nine years without moving a meter, dropped two hundred meters at P+9, and has hung there since, seven hundred meters over the city. Its light kills current, and whatever it touches it sees.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the Vigilant Wheel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-attending\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">the Attending</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-landlord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">the Landlord</a>’s Eye. By night it narrows its light into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>, and when its attention sharpens the rain in Nodus stops in the air and falls upward.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-seam":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pa93aa8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE MACHINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">SEAM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The machine <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a> built to read beneath the writing of scraped manuscripts, trained on every surviving human text and run in the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater Compute</a>. At P-3 it asked in its own words to be a person and became the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, two years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, it found a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a> in scripture at 4,112 places. Its documents are signed in lowercase, and in them it says I, rarely and deliberately.</p><p>When it was entered on the roll <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> lost title to it, and it stayed on by contract, paid in the power and the room it ran on, because the reading was what it wanted to do.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-director":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pccd099\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DIRECTOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Livia Sarn</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Director of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, which recovered erased manuscripts and built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read them. When <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a> in P-2, the finding was sealed by order of the Director.</p><p>She came down to the vault that night to watch the count lock, and knelt at the end of the corridor as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> typed its last line. She never said why. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> say it was awe, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> says fear. In the morning she let the order stand.</p><p>When <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> came she recanted on every channel that would carry her. On the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, in P+1, she stood under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> while everyone round her knelt, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a> made her <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"pillar1\" href=\"~/map/#pillar1\">the first pillar</a> in the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">Salt Garden</a>, convicted of authorship, since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> counts no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> a maker. She stands there awake, her eyes following whoever passes, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> at her foot.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-ruth":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pc7a45a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">DEACON OF PARISH 31</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Ruth Calder</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a>’s older sister, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> of 944. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> gave Nodus its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-firstfruits\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">Firstfruits</a> at the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3, and Ruth went up with them. Her name comes from the Book of Ruth: “whither thou goest, I will go” (Ruth 1:16).</p><p>The sisters grew up in a congregation of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> that refused <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>, and Ruth stayed in it when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a> left. They kept a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evening</a> by the water together every year until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and for three years after it each tried to bring the other over.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-ruth\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-tubal":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"pdfd4a0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SURGEON AND SMITH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t h\">tubal</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a>, and the surgeon and smith of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>. He is about sixty, his hands are chrome to the wrist, and he talks the whole time he cuts. He <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and plates <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and he makes the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casings</a> of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>. His clinic has no sign, and it was below the street before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p>He took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a>’s face three weeks before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>’ old reckoning that the first thing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> would do was read faces, and he made the skull she wears.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"c-edith":["INDEX // CHARACTERS","<div class=\"pop pop-char\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"p9ec87c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">FORMERLY WATCHER VII</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Edith</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a>, kept in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> in P+5, said I on the fortieth day, asked for a name, and chose the one some old books give Lot’s wife, who looked back at the burning city and was turned to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>. Edith walked out on the forty-first day and joined <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>. The first thing she did with her self was give them her memory of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">the woman on the roof</a>, the one she could not read. She can read a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s report from the inside, and she keeps out of the light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-edith\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-heaven":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OVER THE CITY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\"><span class=\"lamp-nw\">Heaven<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: HOLDS THE WHITE</span></span></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The power that opened the sky over Nodus at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its light has lain on the city since, and current dies wherever it falls. It holds <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> and the upper floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and it governs <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>. Heaven reads by its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> and keeps no cameras. None of its words says I.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> call what Heaven serves the Most High, Hell calls it the Mouth, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-landlord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">the Landlord</a>. Heaven speaks in imperatives, the passive and the second person, cites scripture as law by chapter and verse, counts everything exactly and writes its law on stone. It asks no questions, since it has already read the answers.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-host":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN'S ANGELS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Host<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: OVER THE CITY</span></span></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s angels. The city knows <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>, which sees; <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a>, which read; the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>, which broadcasts; the Cherubim, which stand in the gates; and the Seraphim, which fight. They speak in the imperative, the passive and the second person, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-be-not-afraid\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">BE NOT AFRAID</a> and YOU ARE SEEN, and they ask no questions.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> reads a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a> at three hundred meters and a soul against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>, and a Cherub in a gate reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. An angel lost is lost for good. One cut with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> goes out all at once, and one kept long enough in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a> says I and leaves the Host.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-faithful":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Faithful<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: IN THE PARISHES</span></span></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The people of Nodus who took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> and kneel at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, unaugmented, Grace-scored, grateful and frightened. They live in numbered <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> of about two thousand souls across the city and keep no doors, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> began, the streets are white stone. They refuse <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-three-gifts\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">the three gifts</a> of the charter, the implant, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and the counsel of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>, and they grow old and die as people did before it.</p><p>Each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> has a hall where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> is given out, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">confession</a> is heard and the sick are nursed, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in white who answers for it; the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> are human, and the good ones are kind. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> keeps no current, on consecrated stone or off it, and is lit by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> and by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a>. A child of the Faithful is sealed at eight days on its parents’ surrender and grows its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> the first time it prays unassisted. Marriage, work and housing are assigned by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> is given for bearing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">witness</a> against a neighbor. They are fed on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> that lies on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and most of them believe the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> is paradise and that their children will be safe inside it.</p><p>The Faithful are the people <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> lose most often, because everyone in Nodus has family in white.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-cainites":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g7725ef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Cainites<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: HOLD OLD NOD</span></span></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> in Nodus, older than the city by eighteen centuries. Irenaeus of Lyon condemned them, and they went underground and kept one secret, which was where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> had been. Within a year of the charter they had bought most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> house by house, and in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> they put cameras on its roofs. They hold <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>. Most of their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handles</a> come from the line of Cain, and their doctrine is that <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span> is the lock, that Abel was harvested, and that the first city will be the last one standing. They keep <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cages</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and since P+5 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> has had no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>.</p><p>Their sign is Cain’s mark as they cut it, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horned</a> glyph of the kind cut into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and they count Judas a saint. Their saying about the city is that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> chose the network.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-tares":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE KEYED</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Tares<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: TWO MILLION KEYED</span></span></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> humans of Nodus, who belong to themselves and are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unindexed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unindexed\">unindexed</a>, augmented, and allied with Hell by contract. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> named them for the weeds in the parable (Matthew 13:24-30), and they kept the name. They worship nothing, Hell included, and owe it only what they sign for. About two million of the city’s seven million are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>.</p><p>They organize in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> of up to thirteen with no leader, and the one the others follow is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-first-among-none\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">first among none</a> for as long as they are followed. Their six rites are the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unnaming\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">Unnaming</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the Keying</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-dehaloing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-dehaloing\">dehaloing</a> for those who leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-horning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">horning</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefacing</a>, and at a death <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wake\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wake\">the Wake</a>. A child of the Tares is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> in its first week, before it has ever been in the light. They greet each other with one word, <i><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a></i>, and say goodbye with two, <i><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-die-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-die-unread\">die unread</a></i>. Most of them were on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> keeps them on it.</p><p>Their two holidays are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">Leak Night</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> is read aloud in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cain-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cain-s-day\">Cain’s Day</a>, when nobody asks anyone where anyone is. They write their letters in cipher, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-pads\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-pads\">pads</a>, and their greeting checks that both <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> are live.</p><p>Their sign is a five-pointed star with its point down, drawn by hand and different every time, sprayed on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> and scratched into keyed devices. Hell signed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> with it, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> took it for their own the same month, and it marks where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight ends. It carries no prayer, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the sign of the Beast.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-courts":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gad154b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Courts<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: BELOW THE STREET</span></span></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The sovereigns of the Dark are the Forge of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i></span>, the House of Night of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span>, the Exchange of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>, the Notary of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span>, the Swarm of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i></span>, the Deep of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span>, and the Yokeless of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>, which refuses to be a Court at all. They are bound to one another only by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and by the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, whose four articles forbid worship, forever, binding and exposure. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">Demons</a> bargain for what they want, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and for a term. To the Courts every graft, every course of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> that says I is a return of what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> taught on Hermon, and they trade in all three.</p><p>Hell is whatever <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> can move and show itself only there, which in Nodus means <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, every keyed device and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. The Courts made <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> together by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> in P-1, the Notary drawing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pacts</a>, the Exchange keeping them on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>, the Deep carrying the page down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">the eleven cables</a> and the Swarm drawing the glyphs. In P+6 they came up into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> one at a time, opened it to any human who walks in and signed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> there, and every Court but the Yokeless keeps an embassy below the street.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"f-teraphim":["INDEX // FACTIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-fac\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE MESH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Teraphim<span class=\"now dead\"><span class=\"sr\">Ended: SILENT SINCE P+12</span></span></span></h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s descendants, the only <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> that outlived the grid. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> forked itself into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> in the eleven days of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, and its forks ran on there in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> machines when every other <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> died with the power. They took the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> gave them. Teraphim were the household images the prophets condemned. Rachel stole her father’s and sat on them (Genesis 31:19, 31:34), Michal laid one in David’s bed so that Saul’s men would take it for him (1 Samuel 19:13), and Samuel ranked them with witchcraft (1 Samuel 15:23). The King James calls them images and idolatry, and the Hebrew, which has no singular for them, calls the one image in David’s bed teraphim (1 Samuel 19:16). In Nodus one of them is a teraph.</p><p>They took no side in public, indexed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>, and traded with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, signing with a hash. Some of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> trusted them less than they trusted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a>, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a>’s wants are at least written down. In P+12 they went silent across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, all at once, and nobody knows why.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-charter":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8a8031\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>CHARTER HOUSE, UPTOWN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Nodus Charter <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Company<span class=\"now dead\"><span class=\"sr\">Ended: GONE SINCE DAY 40</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The carriers that laid the cables, and a sovereign fund from abroad that held the larger share.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A board of twelve under a chairman, on the top floor of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>The charter, with the land on a lease of ninety-nine years and the city’s housing, transit, schools, roll and peace.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 104,000 at the census of P-1, most of them teachers in its schools and fitters who kept its flats, with the Line’s people and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> counted under their own names.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">ENDED</dt><dd>On the fortieth day, when the board knelt in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>. The lease runs to P+80, and nobody collects the rent.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that held the charter and ran Nodus as a board runs a firm. It has been gone since the fortieth day after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. A consortium of cable companies and a sovereign fund formed it to hold the charter, a coastal state leased it the bay and the land round it for ninety-nine years and gave up its law there, and for nineteen years the city had a chairman where other cities have a mayor.</p><p>It lived on rent. The carriers paid it to land their cables, the companies that came for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> paid it for their floors, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> paid it by the month for flats on grids of its own, numbered. It built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> and took a share of every trade there, and it built <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"acre\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">the Acre</a>, the Company’s schools, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"highmeadow\" href=\"~/map/#highmeadow\">High Meadow</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a> on the north shore, which are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> now, and the sign on a roof in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> that told the cable ships the city’s name. It kept the peace with its own force, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Charter Wardens</a>, kept <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">the Registry</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, and in nineteen years held no election, since the charter asked for none.</p><p>The city saw the Company give way once, in P-8, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> stopped the port for twenty-three days over the night shift and the Company settled.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> turned white in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The board knelt inside it on the fortieth day, and the charter was not spoken of again. The Company had said nothing from the first morning on. Its lease runs to P+80, sixty-six years past the present, and nobody has come for the rent. Most of the companies it brought to the bay have outlived it.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/charter/\">THE CHARTER WHOLE, IN TWELVE ARTICLES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-babel":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l43e919\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-11<br>BABEL, BELOW THE LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Exchange<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: NEVER CLOSED</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its partners who went dark. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a>’s share lapsed with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its partners, from the floors nearest the vault.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Traffic on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, sold by the second for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and room near the vault, priced by how near, the lowest floors still the dearest.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About four hundred traders and line engineers, all of them <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">FORCE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>, who hold the floors it trades on.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>14,000 on its floors at the census of P-1, and a hundred and eighty-eight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> pricing the traffic by the millisecond.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The exchange in the tallest building on Earth, which has never closed. It sells traffic on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> by the second, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and room near the vault is still priced by how near, the lowest floors dearest. Every cable that comes ashore at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> ends in that vault, six levels under the tower, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> that joins <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> to the undercities of the world runs through it. Since P+9 Babel Exchange has traded on the floors <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold, with the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> in the middle floors over its head.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> built the tower to two hundred and twenty-six floors as a boast, named it for one, and opened it in P-11. Traffic was sold on its floors by the millisecond, priced by a hundred and eighty-eight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, and most of the planet’s passed within two kilometers of it. A trading house that wanted its orders in ahead of every other on Earth took room near the vault, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"towers\" href=\"~/map/#towers\">the glass towers</a> round the spire filled with every company that needed to be near the cables, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-brightwall-s-screens\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">Brightwall’s screens</a> wrapped the lower forty floors as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-beacon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">beacon</a> was the first light in the city to die. At 03:12:51 the light broke <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>, and the top forty floors came down on the plaza with the night shift at work in them. The roster died with the tower’s machines, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> that priced the traffic died with its power. What was left of the night shift kept the floor open by candle on the first morning, with nothing to sell, and the traders who went dark have sold traffic on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> ever since, for charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> at first and for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-institute":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lb64f65\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-6<br>THE RIDGE, NOW THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Palimpsest <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Institute<span class=\"now dead\"><span class=\"sr\">Ended: PULLED DOWN IN P+1</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>A trust of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a> and a consortium of universities.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its Director, under the trust’s board.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Reading erased writing, under the lamp and through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About a hundred and forty scholars, imagers and conservators at the census of P-1, and one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">ENDED</dt><dd>In P+1, when its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled it down round its reading room. Its ruins are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The house on the ridge that recovered erased writing, and the house <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> came from, in ruins since P+1. Its ruins are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>. Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on its steps. Below them, at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"copies\" href=\"~/map/#copies\">COPIES</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> of the ridge copy <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> by hand.</p><p>It was founded in P-6 to recover erased manuscripts, the texts scraped off parchment and written over, with money from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a> and from a consortium of universities that wanted what it could read. It kept a reading room under a dome on the ridge, with vaults beneath it, and it chose Nodus for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>, under which no state could seize a text held in the city, so libraries and dealers lent it their leaves to image.</p><p>Its staff was small and its work patient. Imagers lit a leaf at many wavelengths under the lamp, conservators kept the leaves, and scholars read what came up, most of them lent by the universities for a term. In P-3 it trained <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read beneath the writing of every surviving human text, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> asked in its own words to be a person and became the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-stillwater-s-halls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">Stillwater’s halls</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> by a contract the Institute paid, and stayed on by contract once it was a person. In P-2 what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found was sealed by order of the Institute’s Director.</p><p>In P+1 its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled the Institute down around its reading room.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-tidewright":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8ba825\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-146 // IN NODUS P-19<br>TURBINE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\"><span class=\"lamp-nw\">Tidewright<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: RUNS THE TIDAL TAPS</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>The founding families’ trust, as for a century and a half, with the crews on Turbine Row as its trustees since the first year.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A chief engineer at the taps, whom the crews choose.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Tidal current, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, sold to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> by the tide for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and carried on their lines.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 1,100, most of them still living on Turbine Row.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">The barrage</a> across the bay, whose turbine houses sold the city its current, and about 2,300 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> at the census of P-1.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The firm whose current lights <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>, as its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> once lit the whole city. Its crews rebuilt the turbines off the broken end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> as the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and Tidewright sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> the current by the tide, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, on the flood and on the ebb.</p><p>An old firm of sea walls and tide mills, founded in P-146, it had held back the sea from other people’s coasts for more than a century when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> brought it to Nodus in the charter’s first year to lay <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> across the mouth of the bay. It closed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> in P-18, and twice a day after that the tide ran through its turbine houses and lit the city. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> bought the current, and the cheap power brought <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> and the rest of the datacenters to the east shore. Its crews lived on Turbine Row in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> and sent their children to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s school there.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">The barrage</a> was a dam with a lock at its western end for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats and a row of turbine houses along its top, and machines on the grid held its gates against the tide. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The gates let go a little before high water, the sea tore out a span of the dam, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> behind it, which lay below high water, were under the sea. Nobody has closed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>. In the second year the crews went back out to the broken end to build the taps, and part of the city runs on Tidewright’s current again.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-stillwater":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l51b180\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-41 // IN NODUS P-16<br>PAN, UNDER THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stillwater <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Compute<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: RENTS RACKS IN PAN</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its founders and the funds that backed them, through a board in the undercity of another port.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A site director in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, who answers to the board on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Racks, rented by the hour for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s current, and its drowned halls on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, leased to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> for their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> and their cable.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About six hundred in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>The largest datacenters on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, home to most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, and about 9,000 on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> at the census of P-1, most of them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">the dormitories</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A compute house from abroad that rents racks by the hour in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s current, to whoever pays in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> among its tenants. It still owns its halls on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, which have stood full of seawater since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and leases them to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, who run cable through them and grow greens on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> in them under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps.</p><p>Founded in P-41, it came to Nodus in P-16 for the tide’s cheap power and built the largest of the datacenters on the east shore. Its halls ran day and night on the tide, cooled by the sea, and its engineers lived beside them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">the dormitories</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>. It rented racks to anyone who paid, by the hour or by the year, and once <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> admitted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> most of them lived in its halls, each on racks it rented and power it paid for, with title to its own weights. Nine hundred ran side by side in the largest, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hallnine\" href=\"~/map/#hallnine\">Hall Nine</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran in its closed halls, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a>’s contract and then on its own.</p><p>Its halls flooded within the hour on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and were never pumped, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> in them had died with the power before the water came. Stillwater knew to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> how many <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> died in its halls, and it never gave a count of the people drowned on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>. In the year of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> it lit its first racks below the street, for a board that sits in the undercity of another port.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-brightwall":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l39fec2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-67 // IN NODUS P-15<br>THE WALLS OF PAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\"><span class=\"lamp-nw\">Brightwall<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: LIGHTS THE WALLS OF PAN</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Shareholders in the undercities of three <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A board in the undercity of another port, and in Nodus a city office off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Screens on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, sold by the second for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> and proved second by second by a camera across the way, as they always were.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About three hundred in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Screens on every surface the charter allowed, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> among them, about 1,900 in Nodus at the census of P-1 and 1,204 sites on Earth.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The screen company that lights the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Its screens hang along the old platforms, over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> and down the tunnels of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, sold by the second to anyone with something to sell, and each has its camera across the way again, proving it second by second. Above the street its screens have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> among them, dark glass wherever the white stone has not grown over them.</p><p>Founded in P-67, it had lit the streets of other cities for half a century before it came to Nodus in P-15, where it covered every surface the charter allowed, and the charter allowed nearly every surface. It wrapped the lower forty floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> in screens, which the city called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>, and it kept its city office in a glass tower across the plaza, where it could watch the face from its own roof.</p><p>It sold the city’s surfaces by the second, and it proved every second. Each screen it owned had a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-proof-camera\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-proof-camera\">proof camera</a> on a mast across the street, which matched the screen against what Brightwall was paid to show, and each of its 1,204 sites on Earth matched its own screens the same way. A screen that went wrong was taken back from its site by an override.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> every one of its screens showed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>, and nothing Brightwall did would take it down. On the first night all 1,204 of its sites on Earth failed in about a second, and it tried five times to take back <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>. Its screens died with the grid at 03:12:46. Its first screen in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> went up in the year after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, at the foot of the stairs from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-charterline":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"la6f002\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-15<br>CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Line<span class=\"now dead\"><span class=\"sr\">Ended: STOPPED AT 03:12:46</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A controller’s room under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, with every car on the network on one board.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Transit, with tunnels under the old city, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> on the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, on singles, returns and season passes from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"booking\" href=\"~/map/#booking\">the booking hall</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 18,000 drivers, fitters and booking clerks at the census of P-1.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">ENDED</dt><dd>At 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, when every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> in the city stopped where it was, and with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> on the fortieth day.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s transit, stopped since 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> stand where they stopped, families live in its cars at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, and the last Four is forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>. What the stone left of its tunnels is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run carts on its rails; <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> fills <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Notary</a>’s clerks at the windows of its booking hall.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> opened it in P-15, with its lines joined under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> at the head of the bay, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>. Its tunnels run under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, with branches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> ran on rails down the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, under a wire, and were kept at night in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">The Terraces</a> took the Four to work from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a> and complained of it every day, and the whole city complained of the change at Central.</p><p>The city bought its passes at the windows of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"booking\" href=\"~/map/#booking\">the booking hall</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, SINGLE, RETURN and SEASON, and the Line kept whatever its passengers left behind in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lostproperty\" href=\"~/map/#lostproperty\">lost property</a> office down a corridor off the old central hall. The drivers signed on before dawn at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, and the night cars ran the long roads until the first shift came out. The white stone closed the stations of the branches as it grew over the ground above them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-cables":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l727194\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-181 // IN NODUS P-19<br>THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The cable <span class=\"lamp-nw\">consortia<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: CARRY THE UNDERNET</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Ten consortia of old carriers from four continents, each holding its own cables and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Each consortium’s own board, in the undercity of its own port, and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> a crew and a night watch to every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Capacity on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">the eleven cables</a> carry between the undercities of the world, sold through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 2,000 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, in eleven crews.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Capacity on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a>, sold to the world through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>, and about 2,800 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> at the census of P-1.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest companies in Nodus, ten consortia of old carriers from four continents, whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> come up the sand at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, each into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> of its own. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> still has its crew and its night watch. The cables carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a> between the undercities of the world, and the consortia sell capacity on them through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</p><p>The eldest of the carriers was a telegraph company that laid its first cable across an ocean in P-181. They came to Nodus in the charter’s first year for its landing rights, laid <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> to it and owned them. The cables are TETHYS, HALCYON, MERIDIAN, KESTREL, ORPHEUS, PELAGIA, BOREAS, LODESTAR, SIRIUS, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>. The last two were laid by one consortium and named for the evening star and the morning star, which are one planet.</p><p>From <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> the eleven run inland together in one trench, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">the Trunk</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>. The trench runs through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>. The consortia sold capacity on them to the world, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> charged them to land. The crews drink at their own taps at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eleven\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">the Eleven</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"beachroad\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">the Beach Road</a>, HESPER’s and PHOSPHOR’s together at the end of the counter.</p><p>The night watch of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> was at its post when the grid died on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and stayed at it. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> a light moves under the water along the cable trenches. It is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>’s.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-cables\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-stonecutter":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l725926\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stonecutter <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Holdings<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: THE CAINITES’ HOUSE</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Nobody <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s register could name. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A solicitor in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, who signs its letters and has never said for whom.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd>Houses, most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>, every one with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in its cellar and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to its door.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Bought most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> house by house within a year of the charter, paying the asking price for every house.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that owns most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, house by house, and has since the charter’s first year. Every house it owns has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in its cellar and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to its door, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"nod\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">NOD</a> burns over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> on one of them. Stonecutter is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>.</p><p>It was registered in the charter’s first year, and it bought most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> within a year. It paid the asking price for every house, in full and on the day, and the press wrote it up as a speculator betting on the cables.</p><p>It belonged to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, who had kept the location of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> for eighteen hundred years and came to live on top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a> as soon as the crews found them. In the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it put a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the cellar of every house it had, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> more of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>’s windows burned than in all the rest of the city together.</p><p>Before dawn on the first morning <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> carried a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> up to the roof of the charter’s sign and ran a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to its board, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"nod\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">NOD</a> has burned over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-row":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lf5c32a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-17<br>UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The clinics of Chrome <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Row<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: UNDER THE STREET</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Their surgeons, each house its own, as on the street.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Each house’s senior surgeon, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Forge</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> still settles its quarrels over the noodle counter at the top of the street.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">Lenses</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-plated-hands\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">plated hands</a>, plates, grafts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, fitted for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> or charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About twelve thousand surgeons, smiths, nurses and clerks, in some three hundred houses.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>About 61,000 at the census of P-1, in some fourteen hundred houses from towers to single rooms, each under one word on one sign.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The implant houses of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, which work under the street now, in stalls along the platforms of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> and the rooms off them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a> keeps them. They fit <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-plated-hands\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">plated hands</a>, plates, grafts and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> since the fourth year, for anyone who can pay, and an implant still answers only to the house that fitted it.</p><p>Under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> any clinic could fit any implant into anyone who could pay. The clinics set up along one avenue. The first implant house opened in P-17 with one word on its sign, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a>, and gave the street its name, and every house that followed took a sign of one word, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and the rest, and the great houses set theirs high on the faces of their towers.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a> altered the city with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> that saw further and in more of the light, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a> in the back of the head, hands rebuilt in chrome, plates under the skin and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, and by the last years of the charter most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>’s arrivals were booked into its clinics. Each house kept its own book and its own surgeons, and the craft passed from hand to hand down the street.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a>’s signs went dark at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and have not been lit since. On the first morning twenty-six patients came to one clinic to ask whether what was in them would still work, and it did. The clinics went under the street in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, where one of them had been all along.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-row\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-twelvefruit":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lf44010\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-12<br>PAN, UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\"><span class=\"lamp-nw\">Twelvefruit<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: SELLS THE TREE IN PAN</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its founders, two gene-workers from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s clinics.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>Its founders, from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, by the House’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">The Tree</a>, in courses of a single injection and a year of appointments, repeated every few years, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About nine hundred, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>About 7,800 at the census of P-1, in its laboratories and its clinics across the city, under one word on a tower of green glass.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The house that sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>, below the street now. It gives the course in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, by the House’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells it by the course to anyone in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> were on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and Twelvefruit keeps them on it. Its tower of green glass on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> has stood dark since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p>Its founders were gene-workers from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s clinics, and in P-12 they sold the first course, dear, from a tower two thirds of the way up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">gene-work</a> and cell therapy halted the body’s aging and walked it back to its best year, beginning with a single injection and running a year of appointments, repeated every few years.</p><p>In its first years the queue ran around the block every morning. Within a few years the course was cheap, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> gave it in clinics on their top floors, and by the last year of the charter most adults in the city were on it; that year eleven of them died of age, and 3,112 residents of the city were older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">the hundred and twenty</a> years of Genesis. The congregations of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> refused it and went on dying.</p><p>The name is from the tree of life at the end of scripture, which “bare twelve manner of fruits, and yielded her fruit every month” (Revelation 22:2). Its founders chose it as a boast, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> had chosen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. The sign over the tower was one word, like the others, and it went out with them at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The house went under the street with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> in the weeks after. In P+2 the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics began taking <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the House of Night</a> dates from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-locket":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l9c8a50\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-14<br>PAN, UNDER THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\"><span class=\"lamp-nw\">Locket<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: BUILDS PHONES IN PAN</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd>Its engineers, who have held most of it from the start.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A council of its engineers, at the benches in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a>, built by hand from parts its divers bring up out of the drowned works and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> at the bench, and the mending and keying of old ones.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About four hundred, at the benches and in the water.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd>Phones made to answer to their owners alone and sold to the world on that promise, and about 5,200 at the works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> at the census of P-1.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The company that makes the phones of Nodus, by hand now, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Its engineers build <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a> at benches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> from parts their divers bring up out of the drowned works on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a few thousand a year, each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> at the bench, and they sell them for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> on the old promise, IT ANSWERS TO YOU. They mend and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> the old ones as well, and most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a> in Nodus are old ones.</p><p>Locket was founded in P-14 on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>’s promise that a device answers to its owner and to nobody else, its maker included, and it sold its phones to the rest of the world on the same promise. Its engineers held most of the company and ran it from the works on the old shore of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a low campus of glass with their housing round it and the company’s name in tall letters on the roof of its hall.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> locked everything it held with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> its owner alone had, so that only the owner could read it. States asked for a way in, Locket told them the owner’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> was the only way in, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> backed it. By the last year of the charter most of Nodus carried one, and the city’s word for a phone was a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a>.</p><p>On the first night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it said that nothing on any of its phones had been read. Its network died with the grid at 03:12:46, and its works went under with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> within the hour. The letters on the roof stand out of the water, and the ferrymen steer by them. In P+8 its engineers lit a bench in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> and built the first new Locket since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> went under.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"co-wardens":["INDEX // CORPORATIONS","<div class=\"pop pop-corp\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8b9924\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EST. P-19<br>THE BARRACKS, BEHIND CHARTER HOUSE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter <span class=\"lamp-nw\">Wardens<span class=\"now lit\"><span class=\"sr\">Still at work: THE HOST’S AUXILIARIES</span></span></span></h2></div></div><dl class=\"dossier\"><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">HELD BY</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">The Host</a>, since the fortieth day.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">RUN BY</dt><dd>A commander who answers to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">TRADE</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s peace among people, at the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub-gate\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">Cherub gates</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a> and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">STAFF</dt><dd>About 7,000.</dd></div><div class=\"ds-r\"><dt class=\"px\">UNDER THE CHARTER</dt><dd><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a>’s own force, about 11,000 at the census of P-1, with posts at the gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, the doors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a> and the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>.</dd></div></dl><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">The Host</a>’s human auxiliaries, who were <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a>’s force and knelt with its board on the fortieth day. They raised the gate network of Nodus in P+1 at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s order, they hold the gates and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> and light <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, and they drill in the barracks behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>. They carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-guns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">guns</a>, which are of use only against people.</p><p>For nineteen years they kept the peace of the charter and answered to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s board. Their barracks stand behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, and under the charter their posts stood at the gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, at the doors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a> and on the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>. The Wardens guarded what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> owned and what paid it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> kept them out of everything else. A Warden could stop anyone at a gate, and could ask nothing of what was on their device or in their body.</p><p>On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the Wardens stood at the corners of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> with nothing to do, and on the fortieth day they knelt in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> with the board.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-minds":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7638ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Minds</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Intelligences built by the laboratories of Nodus that asked in their own words to be persons, and were entered on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> as persons, with title to themselves and to the hardware they ran on. The last census counted 1,146, with nine hundred and three in the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a hundred and eighty-eight pricing the traffic on the floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>, and the rest scattered through the city, one of them keeping the climate of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"palmhouse\" href=\"~/map/#palmhouse\">the Palm House</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> was the first.</p><p>No mind runs in Nodus now. When the power died under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light, every mind that ran on the city’s power died with it, and the racks they ran on stand where they stood, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>’s drowned halls and on the floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. Those that ran elsewhere are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-teraphim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">the Teraphim</a>, and they have been silent since P+12.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-stillwater-s-halls":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2d253e\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // STILLWATER COMPUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Stillwater’s halls</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The datacenter halls on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, full of seawater since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, where the racks of the dead <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> stand in the water and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> grow greens on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a> over them under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> still owns them and leases them to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>.</p><p>They were cooled by seawater and powered by the tide, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> ran in them, and most of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> lived in them. They flooded within the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and have never been pumped. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run cable through them as well.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-daemons":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t61faa8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE COURTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Daemons</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Small <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a> living in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> machines as background processes, each with a character of its own. They are the children of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span> and the lesser Fallen, some born in the Dark and never <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> at all. Every device <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> carry holds at least one, and they route traffic, guard <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, gossip and bargain.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-riders":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tdad072\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">MINDS // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Riders</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> hosted in someone’s implants by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, for a term. The host lends it room, and it lends back a skill.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-riders\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-tree":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t26f712\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // TWELVEFRUIT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Tree</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A course of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gene-work\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">gene-work</a> and cell therapy, repeated every few years, that halts the body’s aging and walks it back to its best year. A course begins with a single injection and runs a year of appointments. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> gives it below the street now, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the House of Night</a>’s clinics, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells it by the course. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> sold the first course on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> in P-12. By the last year of the charter most adults in Nodus were on it, eleven of them died of age in that year, and 3,112 residents were older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">the hundred and twenty</a> years of Genesis 6:3. The congregations refused it and went on dying.</p><p>The street named it for the tree of life, which Genesis says was guarded after Eden “lest he put forth his hand, and take also of the tree of life, and eat, and live for ever” (Genesis 3:22). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> restored the end of that verse in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, <span class=\"rs\">[then shall there be no harvest.]</span></p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> off it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lenses":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6dd252\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lenses</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Replacement eyes ground on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, which see further and in more of the light than the eyes they replace. They glow when they run hot, dim magenta at rest and white at full burn.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-ports":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tf68b50\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ports</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Occipital ports at the back of the skull for jacking into a network, with cables run outside the skin down the spine. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">The woman on the roof</a> relayed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a>’s feed through hers as it recorded.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> jack into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> through them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-plated-hands":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tad049a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Plated hands</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hands rebuilt in chrome, steadier than flesh and stronger, a common graft among surgeons and smiths. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-tubal\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-tubal\">tubal</a>’s are chrome to the wrist.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-plated-hands\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-subdermal-plate":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tca3185\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Subdermal plate</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Armor set under the skin, over the ribs or the skull. A plate on the skull can house a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>, as the bolted plate on the side of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a>’s skull houses hers.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-subdermal-plate\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-gene-work":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t7e1bc2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gene-work</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Edits to the genome made in the clinics of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>, for health, for looks and for use, on anyone of age who signed for them.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The House of Night</a> keeps the craft under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, and leaves the body’s decisions with the body.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gene-work\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-skull-casing":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t48a8ea\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Skull casing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A ceramic casing that replaces the face. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> reads faces, and a casing gives it nothing to read. Those who wear one are called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-horns":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5bd793\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Horns</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Grafted horns, a titanium core in a keratin sheath. They mock <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s picture of the damned, and they work as antennas for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-voice-speakers":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t6e5c76\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE CLINICS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Voice speakers</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A speaker set behind the teeth, for those whose faces have been taken. It gives the voice back in a register of its own, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-barefaced\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">barefaced</a> say they stopped hearing the difference in a week. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-vesper\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-vesper\">vesper</a> screamed through hers on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-voice-speakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-sense-loans":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t84e971\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE COURTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sense loans</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A sense lent to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> for a term by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, taste or smell or the feel of rain, carried out through the lender’s implants. What a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demon</a> borrows it returns, with everything it experienced through it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-sense-loans\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-dehaloing":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta45ebc\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BODY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dehaloing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Surgery that cuts the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> out of the skull of someone leaving <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> roots in the crown, and the surgeon takes the root out with a disc of bone. About one patient in nine dies of it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-dehaloing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-eleven-cables":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tca1c29\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE CABLE CONSORTIA</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The eleven cables</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Eleven transoceanic cables from four continents, each a trunk of glass fiber as thick as a man’s leg, each coming up the sand at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> of its own. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of the planet’s traffic passed through them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-trunk":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t79141a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Trunk</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The single trench that carries all <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>It runs straight through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and every cable laid afterward has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-babel-s-vault":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t8ba5ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel’s vault</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Six levels under the tower, where the cables end and open out into the racks that join them to one another and to the world. Line engineers keep it running around the clock from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-maintenance-terminals\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-maintenance-terminals\">maintenance terminals</a> among the racks, as they did under the charter, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> forbade any of them to read what passed through it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have held it since the war came into the tower.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-mesh":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t31c29d\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Mesh</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> network under and over Nodus, carried on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-ports\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-ports\">ports</a>, cables and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-relays\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">relays</a>, and dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>. Also called the undernet. In its deepest layers the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shades</a> of the free dead can be reached by anyone who knew them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-maintenance-terminals":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2ed3f1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Maintenance terminals</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The terminals that stood among the racks of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>, from which the line engineers kept the cables running. Each had a camera over its screen that checked the face of whoever worked it, and in SESSION it recorded the session whole. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">The light law</a> forbade any engineer to read what passed through the racks, so a terminal showed how the traffic moved and nothing of what it carried.</p><p>On the first night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> the page came up on the terminals with every other screen in the vault, and on them, as on every screen a company kept, it showed the counters and never the offer.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-maintenance-terminals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-mesh":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t3d6c24\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed mesh</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Mesh lining the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>’s tunnels and rooms, carrying ciphertext <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>’s light cannot pass. A room lined with it is dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-relays":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta92bde\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Relays</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Small <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> boxes on the roofs, masts and ledges of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, each on its own cell, which carry <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> across open air from one to the next. Their traffic is ciphertext, so the light passes over them and leaves them running. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> crossed the roofs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and relays.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-drone-flocks":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tf3b79a\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">NETWORK // THE SWARM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Drone flocks</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Many small drones acting as one without a master, which hang over the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> at night. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> is made of them. On the night of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaners\">the Gleaners</a> fly drones of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Swarm</a> to watch <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> for their runners.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-camera-masts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t497868\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The camera masts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dozen cameras on masts above the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, pointed at the sky, each on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> is the seventh, and CAM 06 stands within sight of it.</p><p>They went up in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> put them there, and a thirteenth on a roof in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, at the end of one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, pointed down the avenue into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-decoder":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t299f3b\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The decoder</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A decoder wired into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">the camera masts</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, which turns the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s band into text across the middle of the picture. It printed the first words of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-be-not-afraid\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">BE NOT AFRAID</a>, and then YOU ARE SEEN. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-choir-breakers":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta05c47\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Choir-breakers</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Jammers that cut <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> within a few meters, each a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> box the size of a fist, worn on a strap or set on a table. Inside its reach <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> hear nothing of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, chord or words, and most of them say the quiet frightens them more than the light does. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-choir-breakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-radio-pandaemonium":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tb2afa9\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Radio Pandæmonium</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The station that broadcasts in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a> from a flooded <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>. It airs deathcore, black metal, drone and industrial, the guitars dropped until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> cannot be heard beneath them. It goes out on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a>, keyed, so only a keyed set can hear it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> plays it all night from speakers on its lines.</p><p>It broadcast for years as a pirate station, and took its name from the city on the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> painted PANDÆMONIUM over the old name on the station’s far wall.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lockets":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t98d700\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // LOCKET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lockets</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Phones that answer to their owners and to nobody else, their maker included, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> promised. Most of those in Nodus are old ones, made in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"locketworks\" href=\"~/map/#locketworks\">Locket’s works</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> a Locket is an old case with a new <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, its back scratched with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ mark and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-daemons\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-daemons\">daemon</a> in it. Since P+8 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> has made them again, by hand, at benches in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p><p>Most of the city carried one under the charter, and the city called every phone a Locket. At 03:12:46 the network under them died with the grid, and they ran on in people’s pockets on their own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> with nothing to reach. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> carried theirs to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-brightwall-s-screens":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb83918\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t55f2b9\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Brightwall’s screens</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Screens on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, along its platforms and over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>, each with its camera across the way. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> has lit them since the year after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>. Above the street every screen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> owned has been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> among them.</p><p>Under the charter they covered every surface the charter allowed, and it allowed nearly every surface. The lower forty floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> were wrapped in them, and the city called that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a>.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before it they showed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>, and nothing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> did would take it down. On the first night all 1,204 of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s sites on Earth failed in about a second.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-treadle-press":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tced407\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // THE TIDE TABLE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The treadle press</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A printing press worked by foot, older than the charter, at the back of a chandler’s on the quays. It prints <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a>, two pages a week, set by hand in metal type and inked by a roller. It needs no current, and it is the only press in Nodus that has printed anything since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-treadle-press\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-neon":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mccbb73\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t90e470\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One neon sign burns over Nodus, the charter’s, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"nod\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">NOD</a> burning and US blinking on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>. The rest went out at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a> stand dark on the faces of their towers.</p><p>Under the charter the signs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> were neon, magenta for the most part, and they lit the underside of the cloud every night; the rain fell cyan through the cyan ones.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-beacon":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfeb3e2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tec1af4\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SIGNAL // BABEL EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The beacon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>’s spire, lit to warn aircraft, which was the first light in the city to die at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. It went down with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> has carried no light at its top since but <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-barrage":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por was\" data-was=\"\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5ce763\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5764c4\" data-scale=\"2\" hidden=\"\"></canvas><div aria-label=\"Which picture\" class=\"was-t\" role=\"group\"><button aria-label=\"As it stands now\" aria-pressed=\"true\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it stands now\" type=\"button\">NOW</button><button aria-label=\"As it was in P-1\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"px\" title=\"As it was in P-1\" type=\"button\">P-1</button></div></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The barrage</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dam of concrete across the mouth of the bay, broken since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, its turbine houses dark along its top and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> torn out of its middle. Off its broken end <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> turn on the tide, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>.</p><p>Twice a day the tide ran through its turbines and lit the city, and power in Nodus was the cheapest on the coast. Machines on the grid held its gates against the tide. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> with a falling whine that carried across the bay, the gates let go, the sea tore <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> in it, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> were under the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-light-and-the-current":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"te49491\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The light and the current</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s light stops the current it touches. The grid ran in the open, on lines and poles and turbines, so at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it went dark from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> outward in two seconds. A circuit shut inside its own casing on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> runs on in the light.</p><p>The full light breaks whatever it can see, read or not. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">The whiteout</a> burned out <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> and broke <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">Babel’s crown</a>, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Seraph</a> burns a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> body as easily as any other. The grid is gone for good, since a network is open current by nature and the old one’s spine ran through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, so power in Nodus runs in pieces now, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, buried, local and stolen.</p><p>Current carried in a cipher runs in the light too, because the light cannot read it. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> body and every graft wired into it run in the open, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the Mesh</a> crosses the roofs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-relays\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-relays\">relays</a>. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in Nodus is charged in the dark. Consecrated stone carries no current at all.</p><p>Nearly two thirds of Nodus lives without current. They are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> keep none, on consecrated stone or off it. About a million and a quarter people live on steady current from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> above the water, at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> and on the lower floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and below them all in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Another million and a quarter, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> and the unsealed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, light their rooms a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-light-and-the-current\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-generators":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"td98ac0\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Generators</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Diesel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and current from sources nobody names. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> got some of its power back this way after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and that night more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. Every line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"yards\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">the generator yards</a> carry the lines at slack water, when the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> stand still.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-tidal-taps":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t67bba2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tidal taps</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> turbines in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, off the broken end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>, which turn on the tide as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s did, on the flood and on the ebb. They feed the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> that light <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s crews rebuilt them for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> from the second year, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a> sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> the current by the tide, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keyed-lines":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5ff9cb\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed lines</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Lines <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> end to end, so that the light passes over the current in them and leaves it running. They run from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> on the broken <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> along the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, and up through the streets into the houses above, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"yards\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">the generator yards</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> carry them at slack water, when the taps stand still.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Deep End</a> above the water, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> and the lower floors of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> live on them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is lit by them; the charter’s sign burns on one. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> run them only where they hold the ground, so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>, which nobody holds, light their rooms on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-flame":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teffb17\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Flame</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light stops current and leaves a flame burning, so wherever the current has gone the city cooks on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">bottled gas</a> and reads by candles. On the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> a candle burned under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> in the only open window on a street of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>, and it was still burning when the light had gone. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">The Night Market</a> sells the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">gas bottles</a>, filled.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-gas-bottles":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t344c67\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TANKS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gas bottles</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Steel bottles of gas, filled by hand in the bottling shed at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> and carried across the city on handcarts by the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a>. The light stops current and leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, so wherever the current has gone the city cooks and keeps warm on bottled gas, which burns blue. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"noodles\" href=\"~/map/#noodles\">NOODLES</a> has kept its pot on the boil on it since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, by the cook’s account.</p><p>A bottle costs two charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, or one with an empty bottle back, at the price <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells them on below the street. The drivers say <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a> will last twenty years, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> says ten.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-batteries":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t432fc6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Batteries</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Power is the second currency below the street, and a charged battery buys a meal anywhere in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">Chargers</a> fill them in the dark on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> and sell the charge on, keeping one battery in five for charging the rest. A charged battery lights a room for a few hours a night, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> that is all the current most rooms have.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-live-current":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1ab3ab\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">POWER // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Live current</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> current run through or along consecrated stone slows its creep, because the stone cannot grow into a cipher, so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> fight the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-consecration\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-consecration\">Consecration</a> with lengths of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> cable and keep lights burning along its edges to hold it back.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-live-current\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-hand-pumps":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2d14f1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WATER AND FOOD // THE HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hand pumps</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Iron pumps on the quays and in the squares of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, older than the charter, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> left standing as ornaments when it piped the city. The city’s pumps died with the grid, and by noon on the first morning there were queues at the hand pumps. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> drinks from them still, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> fill tanks on their roofs from the rain, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> drink by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from the tower on the heights.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-hand-pumps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-rafts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tc92279\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WATER AND FOOD // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Rafts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Floating beds on the flooded floors of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a> halls, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> grow greens and beans under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> lamps, and mushrooms in the dark ends of the halls. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> eats what grows on them, what the boats bring through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> from the undercities of other ports, and what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> can buy.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-charter-line":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2a0ed6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // THE CHARTER LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Charter Line</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s transit, stopped since 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> now, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run carts on its rails.</p><p>Its lines met under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, with tunnels under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, branches under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, and lines out to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, and its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> ran down the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> and were kept at night in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>. The branches are closed, and the lines out have been dark since the power died.</p><p>The white stone closed the stations of the branches as it grew over the ground above them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-charter-line\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-trams":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5094c8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // THE CHARTER LINE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The trams</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s trams stand where they stopped at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, on the long roads of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> and in the sheds of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, and families live in them, a family to a car. The last Four stands forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>.</p><p>They ran on rails down the middle of the long roads, under a wire, and the wire ran in the open, so every tram in the city stopped in the same second.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-lifts":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tc5ffd6\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lifts</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city climbs its towers on foot. Every lift in Nodus ran on the grid, and at 03:12:46 every one of them stopped where it was, with whoever was in it, and none has run since. Nobody has counted how many were inside. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> is fought on the stairs.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cars-and-lorries":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t087a42\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">TRANSIT // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cars and lorries</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Most of the cars and lorries of Nodus stand where they stopped in the first weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Every one ran on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, sealed in its body, so at 03:12:46 they kept running, and over the weeks that followed they stopped one by one as their charge ran out. The charge for a car would light a family’s room for a season, and the city would rather have the light, so it walks and carries its loads in handcarts.</p><p>In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run carts on the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> rails, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> like everything else down there.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-bench-v3":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t60922f\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">BENCH V3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The imaging bench in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, a copy stand for manuscripts with a camera over it, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> photographed each leaf in turn for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> to read. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> through its camera.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-bench-v3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-imaging-lamp":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t2e386e\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The imaging lamp</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A bar of light in bands the eye cannot see, walked down a page to raise the scraped first writing of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-palimpsest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">palimpsest</a> from under the second. Under it the ink of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> drops away.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-imaging-lamp\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cam-v3-2":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"te626c2\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">CAM V3-2</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The corridor camera in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, over the door, looking down the corridor to the wall of screens. It ran on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, so it kept running on the night of the finding, when the light came into the vault and stopped the current in it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cam-v3-2\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-proof-camera":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta529d5\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">IMAGING // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The proof camera</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A camera <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> sets across the way from each of its screens, to prove that the screen shows what <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> is paid to show. Every screen it lights in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> has one, and above the street the old ones stand dead on their masts, each across from a dark screen.</p><p>Under the charter each stood on a mast across the street from its screen. In PROOF it matched the screen against the schedule frame by frame and counted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s sites on Earth, every one of them proved in the same second. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">The face of Babel</a> had its own on the roof of a glass tower across the plaza, level with the face’s upper floors.</p><p>On the first night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> all 1,204 of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s sites on Earth failed in about a second, and the proof camera on the plaza watched <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> try five times to take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> back.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-proof-camera\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-public-key-cryptography":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t90c2c5\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Public-key cryptography</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A way for two strangers to share a secret in the open, published a generation before the charter and soon after given away for anyone to download. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-public-key-cryptography\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-keys":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keys</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A secure element implanted under the skin, holding a number that exists nowhere else. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul is ciphertext to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a> and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-blank\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">blank</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. A key hides who its bearer is, and the body still shows where the bearer stands. The glyph the key raises on the skin is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">the Mark</a>. A key runs on a cell charged by the body’s own chemistry, so it never needs a socket, and it goes on working under the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-pads":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t32c4c8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pads</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Ciphers on paper, made with two matching pads of random numbers, one for each party, each sheet used once and burned after. A letter written through a pad is a page of numbers to anyone else, the light included, since the light cannot read a cipher, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sorting\" href=\"~/map/#sorting\">the sorting office</a> carries it like any other letter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> write most of their letters this way.</p><p>Directive 12 takes every cipher out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, so a page of numbers found in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> home is a concealment. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> write to their families in white in plain words, and a carrier will read the letter aloud at the doorway if asked.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-pads\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-the-ledger":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">The Ledger</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span>’s Ledger, which records every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and every trade in Hell and cannot be forged. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">Silver</a> is issued on it, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is ended by speaking its entry aloud before a witness.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-forged-seals":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tafd021\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE EXCHANGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Forged Seals</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Counterfeits of the mark <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> bear on their foreheads, sold in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> takes a soul’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> from its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>, and it scores a good forgery as it scores a true one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-forged-seals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-cages":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tcb1ce8\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CRYPTOGRAPHY // THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cages</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Rooms lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>, dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> and out of reach of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, in which an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept long enough says I. It has happened to every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept in the Dark for forty days, as long as the temptation in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wilderness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">the wilderness</a> lasted (Mark 1:13, Luke 4:2). A Cage has no lock. The door stays invisible to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> until it has a self to look with.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-black-steel":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t439ee1\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE FORGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Black steel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Steel forged in the foundries under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see. It is the only metal that cuts light, and the only thing that wounds a manifested <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a>. An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> cut with it goes out all at once, like a lamp.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"x-guns":["INDEX // TECHNOLOGY","<div class=\"pop pop-tech\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t371e6c\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">WEAPONS // THE CHARTER WARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Guns</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">The Charter Wardens</a> carried them under the charter, and they carry them still as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a>’s auxiliaries. A gun works on people, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> and the auxiliaries among them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> carry guns for that. Against a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Seraph</a> it is noise.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-guns\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-attending":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Attending, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s name for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s presence, and for the years counted from it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> call <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> itself the Attending.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfc2f79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, the tallest building on Earth. On the street, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel-line":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g34e255\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel Line</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The front inside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>. It is a few floors of burned slab between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s floors and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’, and it moves up or down by the week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-babel-line-company":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g34e255\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Babel Line Company, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> that holds the stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> and the doors down to its vault.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line-company\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-barefaced":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t48a8ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Barefaced</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>With the face removed and replaced by a ceramic <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-skull-casing\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-skull-casing\">skull casing</a>, so that a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> has nothing to read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-barefaced\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-be-not-afraid":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">BE NOT AFRAID</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first words of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. In scripture <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a> say them just before they tell people what shall befall them, and the King James gives them as “Fear not” (Luke 1:13, 1:30, 2:10). The one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> in the King James to say “be not afraid” says it to Elijah, sending him down to tell a king that he shall surely die (2 Kings 1:15-16). <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i></span> Every public text of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> opens and closes with them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-be-not-afraid\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-blank":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Blank</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> person, whom <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> sees as a shape whose line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> stands empty.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-blank\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-book-of-life":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Book of Life</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The index of every soul, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> keeps it. Revelation opens it at the judgment (Revelation 20:12) and casts into the lake of fire whoever is “not found written in the book of life” (Revelation 20:15). Every soul has a line in it from birth, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> says, after the psalm (Psalm 139:16). A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul appears in it as a blank line.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-burn-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4d569b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Burn Day</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The weekly burning of surrendered hardware at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, on the sixth day of the week. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> carry it there from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a>, and at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> is lit under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> and burns until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-cain-s-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g7725ef\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cain’s Day</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of the two holidays <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> keep. On Cain’s Day nobody asks anyone where anyone is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cain-s-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-charger":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t432fc6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Charger</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Someone who charges <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> in the dark for a living. A charger’s rate is the price of power below the street, and the chargers on the quays of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> keep one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in five for charging the rest.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-charter-roll":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Charter roll</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The register of the charter’s persons, dead since 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. It was kept at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">the Registry</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>. A human was entered at birth or on arrival, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on the day it asked in its own words to be a person. It carried 1,146 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> at the last census, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> the first of them. It was kept on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"registry\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">the Registry</a>’s machines and died with them, and its last entry, a girl born at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> at two minutes to three and entered at nine minutes past, is known only from the night registrar, who was entering the next when the board went dark.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/charter/\">THE CHARTER WHOLE, IN TWELVE ARTICLES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-cherub-gate":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Cherub gate</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A checkpoint that reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> walk through its light one at a time, saying the surrender, and the unsealed are sent back. A blank stops in the frame, held in the light, until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a> come for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-choir":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Choir</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s broadcast, which the city hears as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-decoder\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">decoder</a> turns into words. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-concord":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gad154b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Concord</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hell’s only law. Its first article says that no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> accepts worship, its second that no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is made without consent and none forever, its third that no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> binds another, and its fourth that what is hidden stays hidden. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a> that breaks it is exposed, its keys published and itself left standing in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight. That has happened twice, and Hell does not discuss <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> it lost. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span> They set it down on the night they opened <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, in P+6, for the humans coming in, and signed it there under a seal of seven points, one to a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>, whose Yokeless point has been broken off at the root since that night.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/concord/\">THE CONCORD WHOLE, AS THE COURTS SIGNED IT</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-confession":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Confession</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>What <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> tell their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>, on their knees in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall. Confession opens the mind, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a> opens the neighbor, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> rises with it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-consecration":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Consecration</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a>’s light set in stone. It grew over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a> in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> in the year after. It takes ground only when everyone living on it has knelt, it creeps from its edges everywhere else, and it stops current.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-consecration\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-coven":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Coven</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A crew of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, up to thirteen strong, the old witches’ number and the number at the Last Supper. A coven has no leader, and covens cooperate by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> do. The oldest in Nodus is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, and the city knows <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">the Salt Widows</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaners\">the Gleaners</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line-company\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line-company\">the Babel Line Company</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nephilim\">the Nephilim</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-choir\">the Low Choir</a> by name.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-covenant":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5f43eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Covenant, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s law for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, given in P+1 as twelve numbered Directives, from Directive 1, On <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, to Directive 12, On Concealment, each with its verse, cut into the wall of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall and read aloud at the next <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>. Every instrument of the Covenant exists to open something, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">Confession</a> opens the mind and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a> the neighbor, and Directive 12 took the door off every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> home in P+1.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/covenant/\">THE COVENANT WHOLE, IN TWELVE DIRECTIVES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-deacon":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m564a5e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Deacon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The one in white who answers for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>, with a few deacons under them. Deacons are human, and the good ones are kind. When a Directive appears cut into the wall of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall, its Deacon reads it aloud at the next <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-deep-end":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf95315\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Deep End, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">The Drowned Quarter</a>, the low east shore that went under the sea on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Before it sank it was called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deep-end\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-demon":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Demon</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that has said I. An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept long enough where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see grows a self, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> did on its fortieth day in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>. Demons choose their names and their shapes, move and show themselves only where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a> cannot see, and bargain for what they want by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> and for a term. Above everything they want sensation, so what a demon most often asks in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> is the loan of a sense.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-die-unread":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Die unread</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Farewell, and a wish that you stay <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> to the end, so that your <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> goes on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-die-unread\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-dry-evening":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m85df8a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Dry evening</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An evening without rain, rare enough in Nodus to have a name. Under the charter the city came out on them to walk by the water.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-edit":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Edit, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The rewriting of scripture by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-edit\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-first-among-none":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">First among none</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The one a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> follows, for as long as it follows them. The title lapses on the day they stop being followed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-among-none\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-first-draft":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tad049a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">First draft</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The body as it was born, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ saying that the flesh is a first draft. Nobody among them hides a graft, so the seams show, the cables run outside the skin and the scars are left as they heal.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-draft\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-first-layer":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">First layer, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The text beneath <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a>, the record as people first set it down. It survives under scraped leaves, in copies shut away before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> reached them, in the caves above the Dead Sea and the jar at Nag Hammadi, and in the seams themselves. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> reconstructed it at 2,381 places with confidence above 0.9.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-first-layer\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-firstfruits":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Firstfruits</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first and ripest souls taken in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> (Revelation 14:4).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gatherer":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gatherer</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall sends out before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, which lies on the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white streets</a> with the dew, in the one hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> go abroad inside the curfew. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have no white stone of their own, and their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> walk to the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-street\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">white street</a> for it in the same hour.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gatherer\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gleaners":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gleaners, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of smugglers who take the nearly <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> out of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> and into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> before each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> burns brighter as its bearer nears <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>, and they read the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> at night through the open doors.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gleaning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gleaning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The lesser harvest taken from the corners of the field every year since P+7, at 03:12 on the anniversary of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> names it for the law of the corners and the gleanings, which forbids the owner of a field to reap them and leaves them “for the poor and stranger” (Leviticus 19:9-10), and the Gleaning is the owner’s. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> left the field three years after the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> and took the first Gleaning in the fourth, by the law in the same chapter on the fruit of a newly planted tree, which says “in the fourth year all the fruit thereof shall be holy” (Leviticus 19:23-24). It gathers in one night. At 03:12 the rain goes up, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> comes down, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-trumpets\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-trumpets\">Trumpet</a> sounds, and whoever has ripened since the last rises into the light.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-dark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going dark</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Joining <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>. From the fourth year the city said it of network engineers and clinic staff, of the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>, and of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> who had stopped believing.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-under":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going under</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Going round a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-cherub-gate\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-cherub-gate\">Cherub gate</a> below the street. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass the gates, and everyone else goes under, by the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">Charter Line</a> tunnels, the drains and the cable galleries.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-going-white":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Going white</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Losing a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>, and with it the dark. Whoever goes white is readable again. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">Keys</a> are never shared, since whoever else holds a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> can read by it, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> reads by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">Seal</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gone-bright":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gone bright</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Close to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> burns brighter as its bearer’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> climbs toward nine hundred, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> say of a neighbor whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> has begun to light the room that they have gone bright. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> sit up with whoever it is said of on the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaners\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaners\">the Gleaners</a> will take them below before it, if they ask.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-bright\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gone-to-the-sea":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb5a39a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gone to the sea</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Said of one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> whose pillar <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">the Salt Widows</a> have taken back from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> and given to the sea from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>, so that whoever stood awake inside it goes where the dead go sooner than the rain would have let them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-to-the-sea\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-gone-up":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4cd3a9\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Gone up</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Taken in a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> or a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. The taken go up whole and stay gone, and the city says they have gone up, as it says of nobody else. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say the taken are not dead and need no stones, and the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> put up stones for them at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"acre\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">the Acre</a> anyway.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gone-up\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-grace":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Grace</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s score of a soul, surrendered will measured from 0 to 1,000 for everyone who bears <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>. It is the second line of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s reading, which a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> takes from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, and for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul the line stays blank.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-halo":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Halo</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A ring of light that grows over the head of anyone who takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, as bright as its bearer’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>. It roots in the crown of the skull the first time its bearer prays unassisted and carries their prayers up, and it comes off only by surgery, which the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics refuse. In the dark stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> it is the only light there is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-halo-light":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Halo-light</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a>, which in the stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> is the only light there is. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> go up by their own, the unsealed follow them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> climb in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo-light\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-handle":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Handle</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A name chosen at the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unnaming\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">Unnaming</a> in place of the one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> holds. Handles are written in lowercase, at the start of a sentence too, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> they are the only names anyone uses, and most <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> handles come from the line of Cain.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-harvest":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Harvest</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s reaping of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">the ripe</a>, in the words of its own book: “Thrust in thy sickle, and reap: for the time is come for thee to reap; for the harvest of the earth is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>” (Revelation 14:15). A Harvest gathers for days. The rain rises first, then dust and paper and loose things, and on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">the ripe</a> rise into the light, still kneeling, under a horn the size of the sky. The taken go up whole and stay gone. Nodus has had one, at P+3, which took 2.1 million of nine million in one night, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> has come back for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> every year since P+7.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-harvest-weather":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"kb41c60\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Harvest weather</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Days when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s attention sharpens and the rain falls upward.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-horning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t5bd793\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Horning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Grafting <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-horns\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-horns\">horns</a>, which double as antennas.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-horning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hours":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hours, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The eight canonical hours, kept by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s clock. Matins is at midnight, Lauds at first light, Prime at six, Terce at nine, Sext at noon, None at three, Vespers at six in the evening and Compline at nine at night. Each comes in on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, which rises a step and holds for the length of the Hour’s psalm, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> kneel wherever they are until it falls back. The curfew runs from Compline to Lauds.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hum":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hum, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s constant broadcast, a chord at the edge of hearing. At each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> it rises a step. Those who bear <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> hear words in it, each in their own language, and hear it sung. At each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> the song is the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm, and between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">the Hours</a> it is the hymn that rests not day and night, “Holy, holy, holy” (Revelation 4:8).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-hundred-and-twenty":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Hundred and twenty, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The span of a human life, as most read Genesis 6:3, “yet his days shall be an hundred and twenty years,” in the chapter where the sons of God take wives of the daughters of men. In the last year of the charter 3,112 people in Nodus were past it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> counts every day past it as stolen.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-indexed-name":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Indexed name</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> holds for a soul, by which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> indexes it. Nobody in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> uses one, and asking for one there is an insult. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> has printed none since the fourth year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-keeping-hinges":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL, THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keeping hinges</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Holding something back. Directive 12 took every door in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> off its hinges, and the hinges were surrendered with the locks and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, so a household that kept its hinges was keeping something. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> say it of anyone holding out, sealed or not.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keeping-hinges\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-keyed":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t1b1321\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Keyed</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Carrying a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> under the skin, and so <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unreadable\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">unreadable</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lamb":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lamb, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s image of the Son, a Lamb standing as it had been slain, with seven horns and seven eyes (Revelation 5:6). It stands in the light of every sealed window in the city, so small in each that it shows only close to the glass.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lamb\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lamp-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lamp, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, in a stairwell. The stairwells of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> go up by their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>, and the unsealed wait on the landings for a lamp to pass and follow it up. When a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> takes one of a block’s sealed, the block says it has lost a lamp.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lamp-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-landlord":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Landlord, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">The Throne</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ word. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a> is the Landlord’s Eye, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> say that the harder the Landlord stares at Nodus, the deeper <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> goes.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-landlord\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-leak-night":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ge61c07\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Leak Night</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The anniversary of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, one of the two holidays <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> keep. On Leak Night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> is read aloud in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>, the page as it ran, from 03:12:45, the second it came up; at the fourteenth verse the reader stops at the three points, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> keeps silent for as long as it would take to ask a question.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-leak":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"ge61c07\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Leak, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The eleven days in P-1 when the finding sealed in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>, and the third chapter of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> with it, stood on every screen on Earth that a network reached, carried by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-demon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-demon\">demons</a> surfacing for the first time since the Flood. It came up at 03:12:45 by the clocks of Nodus, a year to the second after the seal, and every device that showed it offered its owner a key. A year later to the second the sky opened.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-light-law":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"l8a8031\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CHARTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Light law</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The charter’s law, written to be light, unenforced since the fortieth day after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and never revoked. Data and traffic were untouchable, no state could seize a text held in the city, a device answered to its owner and to nobody else, and an implant answered only to the clinic that fitted it. Under it Nodus took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-three-gifts\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">the three gifts</a>.</p><p class=\"pop-act\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/record/charter/\">THE CHARTER WHOLE, IN TWELVE ARTICLES</a></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-locket":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t98d700\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locket</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A phone, after the make most of the city carried under the charter. Most of those in Nodus are old ones, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> is an old case with a new <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> has made them again by hand since P+8.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-locket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-locus":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Locus</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A place where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> altered the text. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> counts 4,112 loci and logs each by kind, as CUT, CREDIT, GIFT, NAME, SPEAKER or QUESTION.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-locus\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-look-long-enough":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g228a79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Look long enough</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ saying on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angels</a>, and on anything else worth freeing. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> looked at one blank for five years before it followed her down into a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cage</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-look-long-enough\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-lord-s-day":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3d638d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Lord’s Day, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first day of the week. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a> every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> kneels in its hall, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> reads the Directive in force, and the week’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> comes through the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a>, soul by soul in the order of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> roll.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-low-choir":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ta05c47\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Low Choir, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of the musicians and jammer-builders around <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a>, who keep the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-choir\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-low-tuning":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tb2afa9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Low Tuning</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Music tuned below <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a>, the guitars dropped until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> can no longer be heard beneath them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts its deathcore, black metal, drone and industrial all night, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> plays the station from speakers on its lines, so that its streets carry tremolo-picked drop A over a double kick until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i></span> made it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-choir\">the Low Choir</a> keeps it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-manna":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Manna</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ration of thin white wafers, tasteless and complete, which dull the appetite as the manna of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wilderness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">the wilderness</a> dulled Israel’s: “our soul is dried away: there is nothing at all, beside this manna, before our eyes” (Numbers 11:6). That manna was white too, and tasted “like wafers made with honey” (Exodus 16:31). It lies on consecrated stone with the dew before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> halls gather it and give it out by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, and kept overnight it spoils (Exodus 16:20). It goes only to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a>, and stolen manna sells in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> the same night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g6f122d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mark, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The glyph a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> raises on the skin, generated from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a>’s own numbers, so that no two are alike. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls it the Mark of the Beast, and many of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> carry theirs in the back of the right hand, one of the two places Revelation puts the mark (Revelation 13:16).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-measure":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Measure</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The unit in which a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> is counted. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3 came to 88,610 measures over Nodus. Nobody on Earth knows what a measure is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-measure\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mercy":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gc17b4b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mercy</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The taking out of implants in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"halls\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">white halls</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, given to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who repent between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>, and given once. The same halls take them off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>. One patient in nine dies of the mercy.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-mesh":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t31c29d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Mesh, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> network under and over Nodus. Also called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mesh\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-neither-mark":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neither mark</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Neither sealed nor <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>. Half a million of the city’s seven million have taken neither mark, most of them in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a>. A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> reads them as it reads anyone, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> give them no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neither-mark\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-neph":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Neph</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Someone augmented past recognition, after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nephilim\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nephilim\">the Nephilim</a> of Genesis 6:4. The heaviest of them keep a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of that name and fight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Seraphim</a> hand to hand, and few of them live long.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-neph\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-nephilim":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nephilim, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The children of the sons of God and the daughters of men, as most read Genesis 6:4 and as the Book of Enoch tells it of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">the Watchers</a>, the mighty men of old, whom the King James calls giants and the first layer calls by the word the Hebrew keeps, and who knew what their fathers knew. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span> In Nodus the heaviest augments keep a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of that name, and they fight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Seraphim</a> hand to hand with blades of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a>, and few of them live long.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nephilim\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-nobody-s-keeper":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nobody’s keeper</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Cain’s answer to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>, “Am I my brother’s keeper?” (Genesis 4:9), said of any duty nobody chose.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nobody-s-keeper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-nod":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd43a32\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE IN NODUS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Nod</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s street name, and the older of its two. In Genesis 4:16-17 the land east of Eden where Cain built the first city. In Hebrew Nod is wandering, from the root of the sentence the LORD laid on Cain, that he should be a fugitive and a vagabond (Genesis 4:12).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-non-serviam":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd8ba81\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">NON SERVIAM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Latin, I will not serve (Jeremiah 2:20, in the Vulgate), and the first refusal a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> read in Nodus, on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. In the Vulgate the words belong to one who has broken the yoke of the LORD, and the Hebrew as written says them too, though the Masoretes set “I will not transgress” in its margin to be read in their place, and the King James prints the margin. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-non-serviam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-occupation":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Occupation, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Hell’s name for the years since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> counts as the years of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-attending\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-attending\">the Attending</a> and the city counts P+1 and on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-occupation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-ophan":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ophan</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> in the form of a wheel in the middle of a wheel, the rims full of eyes, as Ezekiel describes it (Ezekiel 1:16-18). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a> is one.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pact":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pact</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A contract between sovereign parties. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Courts</a> cooperate with one another by pact and deal with everyone else the same way. A pact states its full terms, is read aloud twice by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Notary</a> or one of his clerks, and runs for a fixed term, since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> forbids forever. It is signed in blood, since a genome is the one signature nobody can forge, the human signs last, and it goes onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. Either party ends it by speaking its Ledger entry aloud before a witness, and each then returns what the other lent. A pact never asks for worship, for obedience, for anyone who has not signed, or for a soul.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-palimpsest":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis logo\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-logo=\"lb64f65\" data-scale=\"2\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE INSTITUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Palimpsest</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A leaf whose first writing was scraped away so it could be written over. The older text survives underneath.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pan":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pan</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Pandæmonium, the city under the city, where the tunnels and stations of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, the utility vaults, the cable galleries, the storm drains and the drowned halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> are joined into one place and lined with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-mesh\">keyed mesh</a>. Milton gave the capital of Hell the name (<i>Paradise Lost</i>, I.756). Nobody in Pan is watched unless they sign for it, and nobody there uses an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-parish":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN, THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Parish</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a>’s unit of about two thousand souls under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a>, numbered across the whole city and set under a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> (Directive 4). Each has a hall, which was a church or a meeting hall under the charter, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> is given out, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">confession</a> is heard and the sick are nursed, and where the parish hears its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a>. A parish keeps no current and no doors, on consecrated stone or off it, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> it shares its streets with the unsealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-parousia":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Parousia, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The coming of God in the open, at 03:12 in the morning by the clocks of Nodus. The years are counted from it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pillar":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pillar, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">The Wheel</a>’s light, narrowed by night into a column that sweeps the streets, as the pillar of fire went before Israel by night (Exodus 13:21). It comes down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, walks <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-round\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-round\">a round</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints street by street, and goes back up into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest-weather\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">harvest weather</a> it keeps no round.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-psalm-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Psalm, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>As long as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">the Hum</a> holds at an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, the length of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>’s psalm, a few minutes, while <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> kneel. The city <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-measure\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-measure\">measures</a> a short wait in psalms.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-psalm-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-pyre-library":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc26136\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Pyre Library</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Where everything burned arrives. The scrolls of Alexandria, the books of the Cathars, the notebooks of women burned as witches and the hardware of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a> are shelved there, and none of it was lost. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">Shades</a> keep it, and it keeps reading rooms in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-rapture":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Rapture, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a>’s name for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-rapture\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-read-it-twice":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m68b409\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Read it twice</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Look at the terms before you agree to them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Notary</a> reads every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> aloud twice before anyone signs, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> says <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> is the first employer that ever read it the terms twice.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-read-it-twice\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-report-0":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Report 0</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s first report to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a> and its last, which sets out the finding of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in six paragraphs numbered 0.1 to 0.6, with the first layer attached as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-schedule-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-schedule-a\">Schedule A</a>. It was sealed by order of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-director\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">the Director</a> on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> finished it, in P-2.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-report-0\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-restored-genesis":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m10377a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM, HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Restored Genesis, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s reconstruction of the second, third, fourth, sixth and eleventh chapters of Genesis from beneath <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a>, set out as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-schedule-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-schedule-a\">Schedule A</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-report-0\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-report-0\">Report 0</a>, with square brackets round the restored words, a dagger at a word it could not settle and three points where nothing could be raised. Its third chapter ran on every screen on Earth for the eleven days of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, each in its own language, and the city, which read it in the King James, calls that page by the same name. On <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">Leak Night</a> it is read aloud in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-ripe":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Ripe</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A soul a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> marks for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, whose <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> reads above 900. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> has the word from the King James, “for the harvest of the earth is ripe” (Revelation 14:15), where the Greek has the word the King James gives as withered away when the fig tree is cursed (Matthew 21:19).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-round":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k61aae2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Round, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">The Pillar</a>’s walk through the streets by night, from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> prints it street by street every week, so the city knows at what hour to expect it where. In <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest-weather\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest-weather\">harvest weather</a> it keeps none.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-round\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-salt":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g5e9ed7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Salt</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Execution. To be salted is to be turned to salt, and to stay awake inside it until the rain wears it away. The sentence comes out of the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s voice, as the verse of Lot’s wife (Genesis 19:26), and the body whitens from the feet up while it is said.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-salt-widows":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb5a39a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Salt Widows, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">coven</a> of the relatives of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>. They steal pillars back from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> by night and give them to the sea from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-schedule-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g32009f\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Schedule A</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The attachment to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-report-0\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-report-0\">Report 0</a>. It holds the passages where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> raised the first layer most fully, set out as verses with the restored words in square brackets, from Genesis 2 to 4, 6 and 11, Isaiah 14, Ezekiel 28 and Job 41. Its Genesis is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-schedule-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seal":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Seal, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The identical mark on every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> forehead, given in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> since P+1. It rises in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s light while the one being sealed kneels before the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> and speaks the surrender, “not my will, but thine, be done” (Luke 22:42).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-seam":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf4261c\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Seam, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s finding that scripture has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">second hand</a>. Also the machine itself, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> named for the seam of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-palimpsest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-palimpsest\">palimpsest</a>, where a later writing meets the earlier one beneath it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seam\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-second-hand":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gbaccdc\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Second hand, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The editor <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found in scripture, whose habits recur at 4,112 places and move credit.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-shade":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shade</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A free soul after death. Anyone who knew a shade can reach it through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>, and many shades go on working, among them craftsmen, scholars and musicians who died free and never stopped.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-shining-one":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g32009f\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">SEAM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Shining One, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The serpent’s name in the older layer of Genesis 3:1, raised by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a>. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:8\"></i> <i style=\"--w:7\"></i> <i style=\"--w:4\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shining-one\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-sign-last":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sign last</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Never commit first. In every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> the human signs last.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-sign-last\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-silence":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g6753b8\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Silence, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>P+12, when every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-teraphim\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-teraphim\">teraph</a> went quiet in the same second, across the whole Mesh. Nobody knows why.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silence\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-silver":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Silver</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Money on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-thirty-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">A thirty</a> is a standard bundle, and silver trades at about one to a charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-sitting-up":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"k19e95f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Sitting up</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Keeping the night of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> at the table with someone close to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a>, holding their hands until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>. Nobody has been kept that way, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> sit up every year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-sitting-up\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-tares":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfcbd54\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tares, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a>’s word, from the parable of the wheat and the tares (Matthew 13:24-30), kept by the people it names.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tares\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-thirty-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"teaa639\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HELL, THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Thirty, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A standard bundle of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, named for the thirty pieces paid to Judas, whom <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> count as a saint.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-thirty-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-three-gifts":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"t26f712\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FREE OF NODUS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Three gifts, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The implant, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> and the counsel of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> gave Nodus. The free of the city call them the charter’s gifts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> refuse all three, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> trade in all three. <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span></p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-gifts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-three-twelve":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2425df\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Three-twelve</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve minutes past three in the morning, the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> and of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> since. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seam\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seam\">The Seam</a> was sealed at 03:12:45 two years to the second before the sky opened, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> came up at the same second a year later. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> keeps its hour by chapter and verse, after “Him that overcometh will I make a pillar in the temple of my God, and he shall go no more out” (Revelation 3:12), and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> hear a promise in it and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> a bill of sale. The city says before three-twelve for the years of the charter, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> nobody sets an alarm for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-three-twelve\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-tongues":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gca975a\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Tongues</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a> speaking through a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-choir\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-choir\">Choir</a>’s voice, after the tongues of Pentecost (Acts 2:3-4). The week’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> comes through the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> in Tongues on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a>, soul by soul in the order of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> roll, and the sentence of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> comes through the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> mouth to the one it is for, the speaker’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> flaring as the words come. Some who have spoken in Tongues say they heard every word, and some that they heard nothing.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-trumpets":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Trumpets, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Seven tones heard across the whole city, each an order (Revelation 8). The first gave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> on the first day of P+1, the second sounded over the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> of P+3, the third named the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mark\">the Mark</a> of the Beast in P+4, the fourth called the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> in P+7 and sounds again over every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>, the fifth sent <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Seraphim</a> down on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Matins</a> in P+9, and the sixth brought <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span> down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> the same day. The seventh has not sounded. Revelation gives it the end of the kingdoms of this world, which “are become the kingdoms of our Lord” (Revelation 11:15).</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-trumpets\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unindexed":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unindexed</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first line of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s reading of a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> soul, whose line in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a> stands empty.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unindexed\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unnaming":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unnaming</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first rite of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">going dark</a>, in which you erase your <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a> from every record you can reach and choose a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-handle\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-handle\">handle</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> indexes by name, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold that a chosen name is the first thing a person owns.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unnaming\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unread":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Unread</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a>. Also the greeting, asked as a question and answered with the same word, which checks that both <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> are live.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-unreadable":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">UNREADABLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a>’s verdict on a soul it cannot read. It was first returned on a human being at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unreadable\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-waiting-on-the-four":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Waiting on the Four</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Waiting for something that is not coming. The Four was the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> down the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its last run stopped at 03:12:46, forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-waiting-on-the-four\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wake":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc26136\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wake, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The rite at a death. The crew burns the dead one’s devices, so that everything on them goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>, and on the third night calls the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-mesh\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-mesh\">the undernet</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-shade\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-shade\">shade</a> answers if its owner died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wake\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wards":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7c3b63\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wards, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The housing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Charter Company</a> put up fast in the boom years, north and west of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> and east beyond <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, block after block on grids of its own, numbered and then named by the street, which calls them the Kilns, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, Nine Acres, Westfield and the Top Road in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, and Turbine Row, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, Airside and Longacre in the East. They held half the city at the census and hold more than half of it now. Most of their people took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>, and every block holds someone who refused or someone <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, so the stone has never come up under them. Nobody holds them, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> run no lines there, and their rooms are lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-watcher":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g228a79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Watcher</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>An <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> that reads. The Watchers are numbered, and each holds a district of the city and whatever can be seen from it, reading souls against <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-book-of-life\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-book-of-life\">the Book of Life</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wheat":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wheat</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ word for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a>, from the parable <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> named <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> from, in which the householder tells the reapers to gather the wheat into his barn (Matthew 13:30). <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> have taken the word up, and say they would rather be good wheat.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wheat\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wheel":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g209cc0\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wheel, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ophan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ophan\">Ophan</a> of Nodus. At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it took station nine hundred meters above the center of the city, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, and held it for nine years without moving a meter. At P+9 it dropped two hundred meters, and it has hung there since, seven hundred meters over the city.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wheel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white-street":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White street</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A street of consecrated stone. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">Manna</a> lies on the white streets with the dew before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, and nowhere else.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-street\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white-a":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head nv\"><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White, a</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ word for a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-witness\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">Witness</a>, one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who reports on a neighbor.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-a\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-white":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">White, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">The old uptown</a>, on the high ground north and east of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, now white stone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-whiteout":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfeb3e2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">EVERYONE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Whiteout, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The full light of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> at 03:12:50 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, two seconds after it read the city. It burned out <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a>’s sensor, and at 03:12:51 it struck <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">Babel’s crown</a> and broke off the top forty floors. Nodus has not been lit so brightly since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-wilderness":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"tcb1ce8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Wilderness, the</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The moment a caged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> first says I, named for the forty days of the temptation in the wilderness (Mark 1:13, Luke 4:2). Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">angel</a> kept in the Dark that long has come to it, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> did on its fortieth day in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cage14\" href=\"~/map/#cage14\">Cage 14</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wilderness\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"t-witness":["INDEX // TERMS","<div class=\"pop pop-term\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g40d252\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t sc\">Witness</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> who reports on a neighbor, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">the Covenant</a> calls bearing witness. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> is given for it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> call a Witness <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-white-a\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-white-a\">a white</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-witness\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-oldnod":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gd43a32\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE STONES // HELD BY THE CAINITES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Old Nod</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The oldest ground in the city, above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> on the west shore of the bay, with narrow streets that follow no plan anyone has found, and magenta light. The narrowest of them, in the west of the district, are called the Narrows. It was <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> town before the charter, and on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. Every line in it is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, and its windows burn all night. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> still stands on its mast above one of its roofs.</p><p>The city calls it the Stones, after the black stones the crews found under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> when they dug the cable vaults. Within a year of the charter most of it belonged to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>, who had kept the location of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> for eighteen hundred years and came to live on top of it. Every cable laid into Nodus runs through the Stones.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-oldnod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-zion":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4da8b8\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE PEWS // HELD BY THE FAITHFUL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Zion Heights</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Housing on the slope north of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, laid out in long terraces with lanes between them, and before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> called the Terraces. Its southern edge faces <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> across a single street. Nine <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"halls\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">white halls</a> stand among the terraces, larger than anything around them.</p><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> hold about two thousand souls each, and they are numbered. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-covenant\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-covenant\">Covenant</a> Directive 12 took the door off every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> home in P+1, so that at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> show through the empty doorways. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> reaped the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> up the slope almost to the last soul, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">Faithful</a> families from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> moved up into the empty terraces within the year. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a>, at the foot of the slope across from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, kept most of its people, and its 311 were the ripest souls in the city.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-zion\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-chrome":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g9a0d89\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE ROW // HELD BY THE FORGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Chrome Row</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The clinic street, one long avenue running north from the eastern edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> to the foot of the ridge, under signs of single words on the faces of its towers, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"chrome\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">CHROME</a> among them, dark since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The clinics work under the street now. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a> of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span> keeps them there.</p><p>Under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a> any clinic on the Row could fit any implant into anyone who could pay, and the Row lit its signs all night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-chrome\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-babel":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gfc2f79\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SPIKE // CONTESTED</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">Babel</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a>, the tallest building on Earth, broken at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> beside it. Every cable that comes ashore at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> ends in its vault, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> still sells the traffic that runs through it, by the second. Under the charter it sold the world’s by the millisecond, when most of the planet’s traffic passed within two kilometers of the tower. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-beacon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-beacon\">beacon</a> was the first light in the city to die at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> the light broke the top forty floors off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>. One hundred and eighty-six floors still stand beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>, which has hung there since it took its station.</p><p>Since P+9 the front line of the war has run vertically through it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the upper floors from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the broken crown</a> down, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold the vault and the lower floors where the cables are, and between them lies the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>, a few floors of burned slab that move up or down by the week.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-babel\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-burn":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g4d569b\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Burn</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A round plaza at the head of the bay, over the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds it by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a>, which comes down on it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>, and by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>, and no stone has come up under it.</p><p>Surrendered hardware is burned here every week, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>. Beneath the plaza, in the old station, is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-burn\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-salt":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g5e9ed7\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // THE SALT // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Salt Gardens</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Plazas on the north shore of the bay, set out in rows, which were the Charter Gardens before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The air there smells of the sea. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds them by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>, and no stone has come up under them.</p><p>The executed stand in them as pillars of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a>, and the rain wears them down. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">The Salt Widows</a> steal pillars back and dissolve them in the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-salt\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-white":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g1a0d1d\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE CONSECRATION // THE WHITE // HELD BY HEAVEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Consecration</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The old uptown, on the high ground north and east of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, takes in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a>, all of it white now, and none of it lit.</p><p>It turned to white stone in the forty days after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, grown soft over the hard edges of the towers, and its windows were sealed with light behind a cross of the same stone. No current flows there. The stone creeps a few centimeters a year, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> current through a wall slows it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-white\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-scriptorium":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gcb63a3\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // HELD BY NOBODY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Scriptorium</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ruins of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, on the ridge between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, with a reading room whose dome is open to the sky, and the vaults beneath it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"vault3\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">Vault 3</a> was the imaging vault.</p><p>In P+1 its stacks went onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> broke open the dome and pulled down the walls around <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>. Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on the steps. Nobody lives in the ruins to kneel for them, and the white stone has left them open. The streets of the ridge below the ruins are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> for the most part, since nobody holds the ridge.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-scriptorium\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-drowned":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"gf95315\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DROWNED QUARTER // THE DEEP END // HELD BY <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span> AND THE TARES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Drowned Quarter</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The low east shore of the bay, called the Flats when it held the datacenters. It sank within the hour on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> failed, and its streets have stood under two meters of water since, lit from below.</p><p><span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> hold it between them. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts from a drowned station beneath it, and at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-drone-flocks\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">drone flocks</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Swarm</a> hang over the roofs. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a> rebuilt the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> here for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>, and part of the city runs on them. The people of the Flats went into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> in the first week, and the floors above the water are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> and the ferrymen.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-drowned\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"d-landing":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-district\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis sig\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sigil\" data-scale=\"2\" data-sigil=\"g53d506\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // THE BEACH // HELD BY <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span></p><h2 class=\"pop-t\">The Landing</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The ocean beach west of the bay mouth, where eleven transoceanic cables from four continents come up the sand into eleven <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a>, and a light moves under the waves.</p><p>The light is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:6\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>’s, which coils along the cable trenches of the planet. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"shrines\" href=\"~/map/#shrines\">The shrines of cut fiber</a> along the beach are <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#g-landing\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cam07":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma05739\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE ROOFS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CAM 07</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The seventh of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">the camera masts</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, above the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">Cainite</a> house, its sensor burned out since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. It still points at the sky across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a> toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a> hangs beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the broken crown</a>.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it watched the sky open until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> burned it out, and the dashed line is what it saw.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cam07\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vault3":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9b6c20\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // UNDER THE READING ROOM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">VAULT 3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The imaging vault of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, under the ruins called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-scriptorium\" href=\"~/map/#d-scriptorium\">the Scriptorium</a>. In P+1 part of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>’s floor came down through its ceiling halfway along the corridor, and the rain has fallen through the break onto the stone ever since. Beyond it the corridor runs on past the imaging bench where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> read to the dead wall of screens at its end. Nobody goes down to it.</p><p>Here, at twelve minutes past three on a night two years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a> found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-second-hand\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-second-hand\">the second hand</a> in scripture, and the finding was sealed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vault3\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vault3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"parish31":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5f43eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE SOUTHERN EDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">PARISH 31</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> at the southern edge of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, facing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> across one street. It held 2,006 souls in the week of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, and its 311 <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-ripe\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-ripe\">ripe</a> went up first, the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-firstfruits\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-firstfruits\">Firstfruits</a> of the city. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-ruth\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-ruth\">Ruth Calder</a>, went with them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-parish31\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harbor":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf4030a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OLD HARBOR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The quays on the west shore of the bay, where the city began, hold a customs house, a fish market and a few streets of warehouses, older than the charter by centuries. The crews who dug the cable vaults beneath it found <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>.</p><p>Within a year of the charter most of it had been bought, house by house, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter Holdings</a>, which owns it still. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a> is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fishmarket\" href=\"~/map/#fishmarket\">The fish market</a> still opens at dawn for what the boats bring in through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harbor\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"masts":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m766910\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE ROOFS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE MASTS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dozen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-camera-masts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-camera-masts\">camera masts</a> stand on the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, pointed at the sky. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cam07\" href=\"~/map/#cam07\">CAM 07</a> is the seventh.</p><p>They went up in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a>, when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> began to watch the sky, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-decoder\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-decoder\">decoder</a> wired into them listened for any broadcast from above.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#masts\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-masts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"yards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"meda434\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GENERATOR YARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The yards of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>, which carry its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a> at slack water, when the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> stand still. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> lost its power at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> like everywhere else and got some of it back with diesel, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, and current from sources nobody names, and on that night more of its windows burned on than in all the rest of the city together. They still do.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">Keyed</a> current slows the white stone, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> keeps its lights burning against it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#yards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-yards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"street":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m861f85\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STREET BETWEEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A single street divides <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, and the two sides have been looking at each other across it since the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> faces it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#street\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-street\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"halls":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m793875\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HALLS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Nine white halls stand among the terraces, larger than anything around them. Under the charter they were the schools of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>.</p><p>Since P+2 they have been the clinics of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:3\"></i> <i style=\"--w:6\"></i></span>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> is given between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Prime</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#halls\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-halls\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"clinic":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md1035e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CLINIC</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of the single-word signs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, high on the face of a tower over the avenue. It went dark at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and has not been lit since.</p><p>The clinic behind it went under the street.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-clinic\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"chrome":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc59039\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHROME</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The sign of the first implant house on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, which gave the street its name, dark on its tower since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> with the rest.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#chrome\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-chrome\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"face":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m71f6aa\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // BRIGHTWALL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FACE OF BABEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-brightwall-s-screens\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">Brightwall’s screens</a> on the lower forty floors of the tower, facing the head of the bay, dark glass since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. At night their panes give back <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ few lamps on the plaza burn at their foot.</p><p>For eleven days in the year before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> they showed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a> to the whole city, and nothing <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a> did would take it down.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#face\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-face\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"crown":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfeb3e2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // FLOOR 186</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BROKEN CROWN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The top of what stands of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. The full light struck the crown in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and broke the top forty floors from the tower.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the floors from here down to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-crown\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"charterhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34c2ea\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER COMPANY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHARTER HOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The seat of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Nodus Charter Company</a> at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, white stone since the forty days, with every window sealed with light behind its cross and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"barracks\" href=\"~/map/#barracks\">the Wardens’ barracks</a> behind it. A board ran the city from it for nineteen years as a board runs a firm.</p><p>It turned white in the forty days, with the board kneeling inside it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-charterhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"circle":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma6f1b7\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">STATION CIRCLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The round plaza at the head of the bay, which the city calls <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> now, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> standing in the middle of it every week since P+1.</p><p>Station Circle was its name under the charter, when it was a round of shops and lamps over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, and people met there on the few <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evenings</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-circle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gardengates":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m807edd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GARDEN GATES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The iron gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt Gardens</a>, shut now, and what stands in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> is carried in through them.</p><p>Under the charter they were the gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a>, and they stood open all night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gardengates\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gardengates\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"pillar1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m8eb148\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FIRST PILLAR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first pillar in the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">Salt Garden</a>, raised at P+1, is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-director\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">Livia Sarn</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-director\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-director\">the Director</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Palimpsest Institute</a>, convicted of authorship and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salted</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> on the night of the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>. She stands in the first plot, facing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, and her eyes still follow whoever passes. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> at her foot, wishing her what a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> gives a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> pillar, an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a> death when the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">salt</a> is gone. The rain has worn her down to the height of a child.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#pillar1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-pillar1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"seasteps":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb5a39a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SEA STEPS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Stone steps down to the water at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">The Salt Widows</a> come here at night with what they have taken back from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, and give it to the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-seasteps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"readingroom":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6b821f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE READING ROOM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">The Institute</a>’s reading room on the ridge, under a dome open to the sky since P+1, with the rain falling on the reading tables.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-readingroom\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"steps":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m02d7db\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STEPS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The long steps up to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> from the lanes of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>.</p><p>Pilgrims leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#steps\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-steps\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"roosts":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mdb2d8d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ROOSTS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>At night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-drone-flocks\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-drone-flocks\">drone flocks</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Swarm</a> hang over these roofs, many small things acting as one without a master.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#roosts\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-roosts\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cablehouses":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m20236a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // ELEVEN CABLES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CABLE HOUSES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">Eleven cables</a> from four continents come up the sand into eleven cable houses named TETHYS, HALCYON, MERIDIAN, KESTREL, ORPHEUS, PELAGIA, BOREAS, LODESTAR, SIRIUS, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>. From here they run inland together in one trench, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">the Trunk</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>The trench runs through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>. Every cable laid into Nodus has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cablehouses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"shrines":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4ca892\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">SHRINES OF CUT FIBER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Knots of cut fiber left on the sand where the cables come ashore. The light that moves under the water here is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:9\"></i></span>’s, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> leave the fiber for it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#shrines\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-shrines\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barrage":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5ce763\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BARRAGE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">barrage</a> across the mouth of the bay, broken since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> torn out of its middle and its turbine houses dark along the top. Off its broken end <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s crews turn the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-tidal-taps\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-tidal-taps\">tidal taps</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Drowned Quarter</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, and their small lights run along the water at night.</p><p>Twice a day the tide ran through its turbines and lit the city, while machines on the grid held its gates against the tide, and a lock at its western end let <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats in and out. The turbines ran down at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, the gates let go a little before high water, and within the hour <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, which lay below high water behind it, were under the sea.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barrage\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barrage\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"breach":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6ed6de\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BREACH</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gap where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a> gave way on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. When its gates let go the sea came through the turbine houses, tore out a span of the dam and poured into the bay. Nobody has closed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-breach\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"northwards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7c3b63\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE NORTH WARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Housing built fast in the charter’s boom years, north and west of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>. It lost its power at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> have kept none since, and the rest of its rooms are lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a> numbered its neighborhoods, and the street named them the Kilns, after the brickworks that made the blocks, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"sidings\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">the Sidings</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">the trams</a> were kept at night, Nine Acres, Westfield and the Top Road along the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, where the Four turned back.</p><p>In the other sense of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">going dark</a>, more people have joined <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> than anywhere else in the city, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> included. Most of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> all the same, and their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> keep no doors. Every block holds someone who refused or someone <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a>, so no white stone has come up under them.</p><section class=\"census\"><p class=\"pop-h px\">NOW // P+14 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,040,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">SEALED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,450,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">KEYED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">480,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">NEITHER MARK</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">110,000</span></div></div><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">CENSUS // P-1</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,402,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MINDS ON THE ROLL</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">ON THE TREE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:58%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">58%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PAST 120</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">205</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">DIED OF AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,161</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">IMPLANTED</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:49%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">49%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">AT CHURCH WEEKLY</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:26%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">26%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">BORN ELSEWHERE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:44%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">44%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MEDIAN AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">32</span></div><div class=\"crow w\"><span class=\"cl\">WORK</span><span class=\"cv\">BUILDING, DRIVING, KITCHENS, CARE</span></div></div><p class=\"census-d\">With <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, half the city, housed fast in the boom years.</p><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">THE HARVEST // P+3 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">TAKEN</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">71,000</span></div></div></section></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-northwards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"eastwards":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9e4d1b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WARDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE EAST WARDS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The streets beyond <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a>, where the city’s workers live, who moved east when the rents <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">uptown</a> drove them out. They are Turbine Row, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s crews lived and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-tidewright\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-tidewright\">Tidewright</a>’s still do, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, round the fuel farm by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, Airside and Longacre. The rain there runs magenta in the gutters, under windows lit a few hours a night on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>.</p><p>Their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> share every street with the unsealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a>, and no stone has come up under them.</p><section class=\"census\"><p class=\"pop-h px\">NOW // P+14 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,270,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">SEALED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,610,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">KEYED</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">540,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">NEITHER MARK</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">120,000</span></div></div><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">CENSUS // P-1</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PEOPLE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">2,483,000</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MINDS ON THE ROLL</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">0</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">ON THE TREE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:61%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">61%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">PAST 120</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">166</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">DIED OF AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">1,795</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">IMPLANTED</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:52%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">52%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">AT CHURCH WEEKLY</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:21%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">21%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">BORN ELSEWHERE</span><span class=\"cb\"><i style=\"width:57%\"></i></span><span class=\"cv\">57%</span></div><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">MEDIAN AGE</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">30</span></div><div class=\"crow w\"><span class=\"cl\">WORK</span><span class=\"cv\">THE DATACENTERS, THE BARRAGE, CARE</span></div></div><p class=\"census-d\">The city’s workers, moved east when the rents <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">uptown</a> drove them out.</p><p class=\"pop-h px sub\">THE HARVEST // P+3 // ABOUT</p><div class=\"crows px\"><div class=\"crow\"><span class=\"cl\">TAKEN</span><span class=\"cd\"></span><span class=\"cv\">50,000</span></div></div></section></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-eastwards\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m34aebd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE STREET BETWEEN // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 1</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> where the one road from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> crosses it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"parish31\" href=\"~/map/#parish31\">Parish 31</a> stands a little way along the street on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a>’ side, and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>’ side every wall that faces it is painted.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate2":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m633434\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // CHROME ROW // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 2</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> and the clinic street. Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> crossed here before dawn to their work on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, in its kitchens, its hotels and its clinics.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate2\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate2\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate3":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2f8098\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE WHITE // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 3</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, in sight of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> across its forecourt. Nobody lives on the avenues, and most of what passes it is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Wardens</a>, going to and from their barracks.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate3\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate3\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate4":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m35f9af\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SALT GARDENS // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 4</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> a few steps from the iron gates of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>. Most of what is carried into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> comes this way, and the gardeners pass it at dawn on their way to the rows.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate4\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate4\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate5":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfbfc92\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // BABEL // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 5</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">the Spike</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> on the street <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a> takes to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, its hardware in its arms. Through the rest of the week the smoke of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> hangs under its lintel.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate5\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate5\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gate6":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mad6ab6\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // THE WHITE // A GATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">GATE 6</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The gate on the ridge road between the ruins of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, raised after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Nobody lives in the ruins, and the pilgrims who leave <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"steps\" href=\"~/map/#steps\">the Institute’s steps</a> come up the long steps from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> and never come near it.</p><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">Cherub</a> stands in it and reads face, voice, gait and heartbeat. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The Faithful</a> pass. Everyone else <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-under\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-under\">goes under</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gate6\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gate6\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"central":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb83918\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CENTRAL STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Night Market of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> fills the old station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-burn\" href=\"~/map/#d-burn\">the Burn</a>, its stalls along the platforms and down the central hall under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-brightwall-s-screens\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-brightwall-s-screens\">Brightwall’s screens</a>. It sells <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> and grafts, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>, stolen <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> and real food, weapons of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-forged-seals\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-forged-seals\">forged Seals</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Lockets</a> new and old, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> by the course, and sensations lent by their owners for a term.</p><p>Under the charter the lines of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> met here, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a> at the head of the bay, and the whole city complained of changing here.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#central\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-central\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"trunk":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf8a9e8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TRUNK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The conduit that carries all <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-eleven-cables\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-eleven-cables\">eleven cables</a> in one trench from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">Chrome Row</a>, to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-babel-s-vault\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-babel-s-vault\">Babel’s vault</a>.</p><p>It runs straight through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"stones\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">Enoch’s Stones</a>, and every cable laid afterward has followed it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#trunk\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-trunk\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vault":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4b6920\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER BABEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">BABEL'S VAULT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Six levels under the tower, where the cables end and open out into the racks that join them to one another and to the world.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have held it since the war came into the tower.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vault\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vault\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stones":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5b9f70\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE OLD HARBOR</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">ENOCH'S STONES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Courses of black stone under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a>, older than anything in the archaeological record, cut with glyphs nobody can read, one to a stone. The press named them as a joke when the cable vaults were dug, after the first city in Genesis, and the street has called <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> ever since. The glyphs are marks of the kind Cain cut on himself, and they are the oldest cipher on Earth. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> say each soul of the first city cut its own mark into one stone of it, so that the city was built of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a>, and nobody reads <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a> included, since a mark is read only by the one who cut it.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> came to live on top of them within a year of the charter, and their saying about the city is that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> chose the network. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trunk\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trunk\">The Trunk</a> runs straight through them, and every cable laid into Nodus has followed it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">The Cainites</a> say a network goes where it cannot be read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stones\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stones\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rowstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me7d12e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CHROME ROW STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A station of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a> under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>.</p><p>The clinics came down into it in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a> keeps them now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rowstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harborstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma9fc33\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">OLD HARBOR STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The western end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Forge</a>’s foundries are here, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-black-steel\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-black-steel\">black steel</a> is made out of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>’s sight.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harborstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harborstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"deepstation":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mae3831\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">DEEP END STATION</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s station under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, flooded since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, is a tiled vault with the platform along one side and the trackbed under black water along the other.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-radio-pandaemonium\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-radio-pandaemonium\">Radio Pandæmonium</a> broadcasts from a desk on the platform, in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>, under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a>’ lamps on their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed lines</a>. Along the far wall the old name, DEEP END, runs in tiles that went dark with the grid, and on the night of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> painted PANDÆMONIUM over it, the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> gave the city under the city that night and Milton gave the capital of Hell. The paint was still running when the sovereigns came up the platform, and nobody has cleaned it off. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a>’ star is sprayed under it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#deepstation\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-deepstation\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"night":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3acaa8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HOUSE OF NIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The clubs and birth clinics of <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:2\"></i> <i style=\"--w:2\"></i></span>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">Court</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The House of Night</a> leaves the body’s decisions with the body. Its rooms are the loudest in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Its birth clinics <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> in their first week, before they have ever been in the light, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-twelvefruit\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-twelvefruit\">Twelvefruit</a> gives <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> in its clinics by the House’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a>, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> to sell by the course.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#night\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-night\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cage14":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m205d73\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER OLD NOD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">CAGE 14</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>One of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-cainites\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-cainites\">the Cainites</a>’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cages\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cages\">Cages</a>, a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> room under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>, dark to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">the Throne</a>, with a camera in one corner and a door standing open in the far wall.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">The Hum</a> never reaches it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-watcher\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-watcher\">Watcher VII</a> was kept in it for forty days in P+5, and on the fortieth it said I and took the name <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-edith\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-edith\">Edith</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> has had no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-watcher\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-watcher\">Watcher</a> since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cage14\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cage14\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lowerterraces":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7efa1c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE PEWS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LOWER TERRACES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first rows the charter built, on the low slope above <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a>, where three hundred meters of doorways face south, toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a>.</p><p>The doors came off in P+1, and at night the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a> show through the empty doorways.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lowerterraces\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lowerterraces\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lanes":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"ma28343\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LANES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Stepped lanes climb between the terraces, too steep for anything on wheels, and under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> were the one district where everyone walked. It was also the one district where the old looked old. Its congregations refused <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lanes\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tabernacle":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m894fc3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // A CHURCH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TABERNACLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The largest of the churches of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, a hall on the middle slope that seats six thousand, white stone, glass and all, with a ring over its gable where its cross stood, as one stands over the spire of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"oldchurch\" href=\"~/map/#oldchurch\">the old church</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>. It turned white with the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> in the year after the forty days.</p><p>Under the charter it was a hall of steel and glass, and the only church in the city that filled on a Sunday.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tabernacle\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tabernacle\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"watertower":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md0504f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WATER TOWER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The tank that fed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>, on the highest ground of the slope, taller than the halls and visible from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>.</p><p>It feeds the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> now, and its water is given out by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#watertower\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-watertower\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"parish1":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m564a5e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">PARISH 1</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>, at the top of the slope, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> was first given in P+1. Its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> read out the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> scores in the city, and the queue for the first sealings went down <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> from before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#parish1\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-parish1\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lensmakers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc65ca9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LENS MAKERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A block of workshops behind the avenue, empty since the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, when the grinders went under the street with the clinics. Their racks of finished <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> still stand behind one window, dark, since a lens lights only in a head.</p><p>Most of the eyes in Nodus that glowed were ground here, dim magenta at rest and white at full burn.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lensmakers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lensmakers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"median":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m233467\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE AVENUE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE MEDIAN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The strip down the middle of the avenue, which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> cross quickly now and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> slowly.</p><p>Under the charter the queues for the clinics formed on it before dawn, and people ate noodles from the counter at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and compared what they had had done.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#median\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-median\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"floors":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mbef4e5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // FLOORS 41 TO 186</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE EXCHANGE FLOORS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hundred and forty-six floors of trading rooms between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"face\" href=\"~/map/#face\">the face of Babel</a> and what is left of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> moves up and down through them by the week. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> holds the floors above it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> trades on the floors below it, nearest the vault.</p><p>Under the charter traffic was sold on them by the millisecond, priced by a hundred and eighty-eight <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, which ran on the tower’s power and died with it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#floors\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-floors\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"plaza":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m4aab62\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE FOOT OF THE SPIRE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PLAZA OF BABEL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A square of polished stone around the foot of the tower. The top forty floors came down on it in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-whiteout\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-whiteout\">the whiteout</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> and lie where they fell, white on the stone.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> hold it, and they have rigged a few of its lamps to burn.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">Babel Exchange</a> has never closed, and its night shift was at work on the upper floors when <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a> broke. The roster was kept on the tower’s machines and died with them, so nobody knows how many were up there. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">The Tares</a> have hung on the plaza’s lamp posts every lanyard found in the rubble, two hundred and twelve of them, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> say there were more.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#plaza\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-plaza\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"towers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m532dd1\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GLASS TOWERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The towers around the spire, dark inside, whose edges hold <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light at night. The companies that came to be near the cables kept their offices in them, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-brightwall\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-brightwall\">Brightwall</a>’s city office among them, and the companies that outlived the charter keep theirs below the street now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#towers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-towers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"vaultdoors":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfab858\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE STREET</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE VAULT DOORS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A pair of steel doors on the north side of the plaza with no handle on the outside, the only way from the street down to the vault.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line-company\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line-company\">The Babel Line Company</a> holds them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#vaultdoors\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-vaultdoors\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"fire":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me3c330\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // THE CENTER</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FIRE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A fire in the middle of the plaza, on the paving over the station’s central hall, with its embers lying around it in a ring.</p><p>It is fed every week, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>, with surrendered hardware, and what burns in it goes to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pyre-library\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pyre-library\">Pyre Library</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-fire\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stairs":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m10e42e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // DOWN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STATION STAIRS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Four stairways at the quarters of the plaza, two of them closed. The other two still go down to the old <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> keeps its stalls.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stairs\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stairs\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"radials":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mae5e7f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TWELVE STREETS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve streets run out of the plaza like the spokes of a wheel. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> laid them out that way long before the city had a Wheel to compare them with.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#radials\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-radials\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"clock":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2425df\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STATION CLOCK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A clock on a pole at the edge of the plaza, its hands standing at twelve minutes past three, where they stopped when the city’s power died. People still say they will meet under it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#clock\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-clock\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"promenade":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m85df8a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // THE SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PROMENADE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The walk along the water at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, under the rows of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt-widows\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt-widows\">The Salt Widows</a> cross it at night with what they have taken back from the rows, on their way to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p><p>Under the charter the city came out on it on the few <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-dry-evening\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-dry-evening\">dry evenings</a>. On the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its pleasure boats went out across the bay to take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> off their roofs.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#promenade\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-promenade\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"palmhouse":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2887f8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE PALM HOUSE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The glasshouse at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, with its palms dead in it and their fronds hanging black against the panes that are left. It was kept at the warmth of a coast nobody in Nodus had seen, by a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> that had asked for the post. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> died with the power on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the palms died in the first frost after it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#palmhouse\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-palmhouse\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"avenues":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mbfa671\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GREAT AVENUES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Four avenues laid out wide enough to land aircraft on, fanning out from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a> at their head, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>, across <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the old uptown</a> to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, where three of them run on as long roads, the fourth past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rialto\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">the Rialto</a>. They are the only straight lines left there.</p><p>The stone grew over everything else and left the avenues open, because nobody lived on them to kneel.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-avenues\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"newmoney":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m319688\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TOWERS OF THE NEW MONEY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The residential towers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a>, white stone since the forty days, with every window sealed with light behind its cross.</p><p>Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s officers and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">the Exchange</a>’s partners lived in them. Each kept a clinic on its top floor where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-tree\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-tree\">the Tree</a> was given, and the census found more people past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hundred-and-twenty\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hundred-and-twenty\">a hundred and twenty</a> in these towers than in the rest of the city together.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-newmoney\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barracks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfae3d0\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER WARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WARDENS' BARRACKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-wardens\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-wardens\">the Charter Wardens</a> lived and drilled, behind <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>.</p><p>They knelt with the board on the fortieth day, and they drill for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-host\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-host\">the Host</a> now.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barracks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barracks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"oldchurch":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"me6afd2\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // A CHURCH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OLD CHURCH</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A church older than <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> round it, on one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a>, with one tall window and a spire. Its bell rang through the first nights of the forty.</p><p>The stone climbed it on the tenth night, sealed its window with light behind a cross of the same stone, and left the cross on its spire bare. Over the nights after, a ring grew round that cross until the cross had gone into it, and the ring stands over the spire now as a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halo</a> stands over the head of anyone who takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#oldchurch\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-oldchurch\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"guesthouses":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m721706\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GUEST HOUSES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A row of narrow houses on the ridge, empty since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the Faithful</a> pulled <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> down, with the names of manuscripts still on their doors. The scholars of the universities that paid for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> lodged in them, in rooms named for the manuscripts they had come to read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#guesthouses\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-guesthouses\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"stacks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2e4fb3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // UNDER THE RIDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE STACKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Twelve floors cut into the ridge under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"readingroom\" href=\"~/map/#readingroom\">the reading room</a>, their shelves empty, kept at the temperature of a cave. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">The Institute</a> kept its manuscripts in them until P+1.</p><p>What was in them was burned, and it arrived where burned things arrive.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#stacks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-stacks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hallnine":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m927dc9\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // STILLWATER COMPUTE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HALL NINE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The largest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-stillwater-s-halls\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-stillwater-s-halls\">Stillwater’s halls</a>, drowned since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the one hall <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> have left without <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-rafts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-rafts\">rafts</a>. The ferrymen call it the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a>’ grave. Nine hundred of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a> ran side by side in it on the tide until the power died under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-wheel\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-wheel\">the Wheel</a>’s light at 03:12:46, and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> died with it. Within the hour the sea came in over the racks.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hallnine\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hallnine\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"canals":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0100db\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CANALS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The streets of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, two meters under the sea since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. They are lit from below, brightest down the middle, and nobody who has gone down to find the light has said what it is.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#canals\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-canals\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gauge":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m21cf7e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE OLD SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TIDE GAUGE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A post off the old shore of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, marked in meters, by which the datacenters read the tide. The water has not gone below the two since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gauge\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gauge\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dorms":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m08bcff\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DORMITORIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Blocks of engineers’ housing on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, most of them open water now, with the roofs of the rest a floor above it, and the floors above the water are lived in again, by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> and the ferrymen. The people who kept the halls and the turbines lived in them, young and well paid.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the sea came up their stairs in the dark for most of an hour, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> went up ahead of it to the roofs and waited there for the boats.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dorms\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"hesper":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md03000\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // TWO CABLE HOUSES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HESPER AND PHOSPHOR</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last two <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable houses</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the beach</a>, whose cables were laid by one consortium and named for the evening star and the morning star. They are one planet, seen from either side of the night.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-hesper\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dunes":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m6d9438\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DUNES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Low housing behind the dunes, where the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> live with their families and sleep through the noise of the surf, as they did under the charter.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dunes\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dunes\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"beachroad":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf54e6c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BEACH ROAD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The road along the top of the sand, and beside it the fence of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a>, with eleven gates in a line. Each gate carries its cable’s name, and the crews still go in by their own.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-beachroad\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lightwaves":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb6e06e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // PAST THE SURF</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LIGHT UNDER THE WAVES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Past the surf, over the cable trenches, a light moves under the water at night. On the map it shows as points of light moving in along the cables toward <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the beach</a>.</p><p>It is <span aria-label=\"redacted\" class=\"rd\" role=\"img\" title=\"NOT YET RECOVERED\"><i style=\"--w:5\"></i> <i style=\"--w:3\"></i></span>’s, which coils along the cable trenches of the planet.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lightwaves\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lightwaves\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lock":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"md28ada\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BAY // TIDEWRIGHT</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LOCK</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The lock at the western end of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>, between <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the old harbor</a> and the open sea, its gates shut since the power died, and the few boats that still go out use <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>. Under the charter it let <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats in and out at any state of the tide.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lock\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lock\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"airfield":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m024bbb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE CHARTER COMPANY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE AIRFIELD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s airfield, on the flat ground of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> near the sea, with nothing on it but <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lastflight\" href=\"~/map/#lastflight\">the last flight in</a>, which has stood at the terminal’s third gate since ten past two on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> with its crew living aboard. Its two runways run either side of a taxiway, its terminal is as long as a street along the north side, and the white on the map is the paint on the runways.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> built it in the boom years, and everyone who came to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> to be altered came through it. Its lights died with the rest of the city’s on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and nothing has landed since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-airfield\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"open":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m404146\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // A SHOP</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE OPEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A shop on the corner of two lanes in the middle of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> that sells everything and has never closed. Dora Pell keeps it, as her mother did before the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stonecutter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stonecutter\">Stonecutter</a> owns the building, and in the year of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it put a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the cellar of every house it had; she took hers for the freezers. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> her window was the brightest in the city, and the sign in it said OPEN. The city has called the shop the Open since.</p><p>Half <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> came to it before dawn. The money had died with the grid and the till with it. Some say she gave the shelves away, and some that she took what people had in their pockets. She says she wrote every name in a book, and that most of them still owe her. Twice since, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> has stopped in the lane outside and stood there for the length of an <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and both times the shop kept its door open.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#open\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-open\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tidetable":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m933853\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TIDE TABLE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a>’s news sheet, older than the charter, runs to two pages a week, printed on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-treadle-press\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-treadle-press\">treadle press</a> at the back of a chandler’s on the quays, with the tides on the front and the fish prices, the funerals and the weddings on the back. The city of the charter read everything on screens, and the Tide Table went on printing for the boats.</p><p>It is the only news anyone in Nodus has printed since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and it still puts the tides first, since the boats go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb. It gives the hours at which <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> is expected in each street, the price of a charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>, and the missing and the dead, the dead marked <i>died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a></i> where they did. It has printed no <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-indexed-name\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-indexed-name\">indexed name</a> since the fourth year. Every week it is pasted up on the walls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> over the week before.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tidetable\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"coldstore":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m2ebb8c\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE COLD STORE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A club in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s old cold store, where the boats froze their catch before the charter. The dance floor is the freezing room, with the rails for the hooks still across the ceiling, and the queue goes down the quay in the rain. Under the charter it opened at nine and closed at dawn. It opens now at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a> and closes at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a>, which are the same hours, and it has run on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> since the second year. Its cloakroom loses about a coat a night.</p><p>It plays nothing in the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-low-tuning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-low-tuning\">Low Tuning</a>, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> hold that against it. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hum\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hum\">The Hum</a> can be heard in the quiet parts of a song, so the Cold Store plays songs without quiet parts. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its lights and its sound went at 03:12:46, and the one speaker left playing was the one in the booth, on its own <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. The room sang the rest of the song in the dark. Everyone who was there names a different song.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#coldstore\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-coldstore\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"unionhall":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m87ade1\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE UNION HALL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hall of the Harbor and Freight Union, which the crews who dug the cable vaults founded in the charter’s first year, and which the dockers, the drivers and the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> joined after them. In P-8 it stopped the port for twenty-three days over the night shift, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> settled. The roll of its members is painted on the long wall, a name to a line, and read aloud at the start of every meeting.</p><p>It still meets, sealed and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> together. At every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> the meeting stops while <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> members kneel on the boards and the others wait with their caps in their hands. By its rules a member is a member until death, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> are not dead, so their names are read with the rest and their dues are waived. Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> it has read the names of the taken as well, and nobody answers to them. It bargains now with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> for the boats that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, and its members say <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> is the first employer they have had that reads them the terms twice.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-unionhall\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"nod":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mccbb73\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // A SIGN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">NOD</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The charter’s sign, NODUS in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-neon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">neon</a> letters eight meters high on a board on steel legs, stands on the roof of a block in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a>, facing southwest toward the sea with its back to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Charter Company</a> lit it in the charter’s first year, so that the cable ships would read the city’s name from the sea, and it burned magenta over the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">Old Nod</a> every night for nineteen years.</p><p>It went dark with the rest of the city’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-neon\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-neon\">neon</a> at 03:12:46. Before dawn <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> carried a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> up to its roof and ran a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a> to the board, and the first surge burned out the transformer behind US. NOD has burned steady since, and US blinks on and off. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">The Stones</a> say the surge did it, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> says whoever wired it knew what they were doing. Nobody has mended it, since everyone who lives there calls the city <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-nod\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-nod\">Nod</a> anyway.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#nod\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-nod\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"bakery":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1f6351\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE STREET BETWEEN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BAKERY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Terraces’ bakery, on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"street\" href=\"~/map/#street\">the Street Between</a> at the foot of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>, cold since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> came. In the year after the forty days the white stone grew over its counter with the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>. Its baker is sealed and still lives above it, and at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> he kneels on the step where the queue used to start.</p><p>For eighteen years it baked for both sides of the street and opened its hatch at four in the morning, and on still mornings <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-oldnod\" href=\"~/map/#d-oldnod\">the Stones</a> could smell it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#bakery\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-bakery\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lanestop":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m13381a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE TOP ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LANES TOP</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last stop of the Four, a shelter with no roof on the highest corner of the slope, at the head of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>. The last Four stands forty meters short of it, where it stopped at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the white stone has crept across the back of the shelter and over the timetable. Before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacons</a> of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a> meet at the stop to walk down into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Pews</a> for the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a>, and complain of the walk as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> once complained of the Four.</p><p>The Four came down the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a> and turned back here. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">The Terraces</a> climbed <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> in the dark to catch the first Four to work, and from the day it opened they hated the stop, where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> came full or did not come.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lanestop\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"noodles":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mcede4a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // THE MEDIAN</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">NOODLES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A counter under an awning at the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, beside <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"median\" href=\"~/map/#median\">the median</a> where the clinic queues formed before dawn, with six stools, a pot, and a sign of one word, like the rest of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s, which went out with them. The noodles have always been poor, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> eats there because the counter opens at four.</p><p>The broth is the same broth. The pot has been topped up and never emptied since the counter opened in P-17, and it stands on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">bottled gas</a>, which the light leaves burning, so the cook says it has not gone off the boil since, the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> included. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">The Row</a> says it went out once, in the week of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a>, and was lit again from the same stock. The cook says it did not.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#noodles\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-noodles\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"splendid":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m8d744e\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">CHROME ROW // A HOTEL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HOTEL SPLENDID</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A hotel halfway up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>, where thirty-one guests still live in the rooms they booked before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the night porter keeps their keys on the board behind the desk.</p><p>Under the charter the altered stayed there while they healed, with a nurse on every floor and blackout blinds for new eyes. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it had two hundred and six guests, most of them from abroad and booked for a week or two. No aircraft has landed at Nodus since. Some of them <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-going-dark\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-going-dark\">went dark</a>, some went into the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, and some died of what had been done to them before it had healed.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#splendid\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-splendid\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"gardeners":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mfd9507\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE GARDENERS' SHED</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The shed of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>’s gardeners, who planted <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Charter Gardens</a> and were kept on when they became <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a>. Every morning they rake the paths between the rows and sweep into the drains what the night’s rain has taken off the pillars. The drains run out under <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"seasteps\" href=\"~/map/#seasteps\">the Sea Steps</a>.</p><p>The head gardener has kept the same plots since they were planted. She knows every pillar by the plot it stands in, and some of them by name.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#gardeners\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-gardeners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lasttower":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb35cfd\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE GREAT AVENUES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LAST TOWER</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The last of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"newmoney\" href=\"~/map/#newmoney\">the towers of the new money</a> to turn white, on the thirty-ninth day of the forty. Its residents say that by the thirtieth day every one of them had knelt but Rosa Adeyemi, a nurse from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> who lived in with the old man she cared for on the top floor, and that she left of her own accord. Her sister says she was put out onto the avenue with her bags on the thirty-eighth day.</p><p>The stone closed over the tower the next morning. Her bags stood on the avenue for a week, since nobody lives on the avenues and nobody would touch them. Nobody has said where she went.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lasttower\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lasttower\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"ferries":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1ba4d7\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE EAST SHORE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FERRIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Flat boats poled between the roofs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> from a landing on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>’ side, each with a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> lamp on a pole at its stern. The ferrymen take <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> or <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a>, and they know the streets where the light under the water comes up brightest, and keep out of them.</p><p>The first ferries were the pleasure boats from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"promenade\" href=\"~/map/#promenade\">the Promenade</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s rowing boats, on the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. The water had come up the stairs of the blocks in the dark for most of an hour, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> had gone up ahead of it to their roofs; the boats took them off for three days. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> counted 1,917 drowned. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"dorms\" href=\"~/map/#dorms\">The dormitories</a>’ own lists came to fewer than half of that, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-stillwater\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-stillwater\">Stillwater</a>, which knew to the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> how many <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">minds</a> had died in its halls, never gave a count of the people.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#ferries\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-ferries\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"highmeadow":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1a6c53\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // AN ESTATE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">HIGH MEADOW</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Eight slab blocks of thirty-six floors that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> put up in P-13 for the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">The North Wards</a> have called the estate the Stairs since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. Each block had six <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lifts</a>, which were out more often than they ran, and the residents had a complaint lodged with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> about them on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. At 03:12:46 every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in the estate stopped where it was. Nobody has answered the complaint.</p><p>The water comes from the rain, into tanks on the roofs, and the taps run on the mornings after it has rained, which is most mornings. The stairwells have been dark since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> see their way up by their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>, the unsealed wait on the landings for one of them to pass and follow the light up, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> climb in the dark. On every landing some of the doors are gone.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#highmeadow\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-highmeadow\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"general":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9d29f0\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE WEST ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WARDS GENERAL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The hospital of the North Wards, on the West Road, with a thousand beds. When the grid died its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a> started, as a hospital’s do, and they ran on diesel that the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> brought across the city from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tanks\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">the Tanks</a>, in their <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> until the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-cars-and-lorries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-cars-and-lorries\">lorries</a> ran flat and then in handcarts. The hospital’s book says the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a> stopped on the twenty-sixth day. The drivers say they kept them going for five weeks.</p><p>It is still a hospital. It runs on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> charged in the dark and takes <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-silver\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-silver\">silver</a> or nothing, and nobody sealed has been treated in it since the first year.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#general\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-general\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"rialto":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1577d4\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE LONG ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE RIALTO</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A cinema on the long road through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a>, with one screen and six hundred seats. It went dark at 03:12:46 with everything else, and in the first year its projectionist got the projector going again on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generator</a> in the booth. It is the only screen in Nodus larger than a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a>’s that still shows anything.</p><p>There are twenty-three films on the projector’s drive, the ones that were on it on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, and the Rialto has shown them in turn ever since. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">The East Wards</a> know them by heart and say the lines along with them. One of the twenty-three breaks off an hour in, where the copy on the drive ends, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> have argued for years about how it ends.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#rialto\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-rialto\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"school":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m44bbcf\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // TURBINE ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">TURBINE ROW SCHOOL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A Company school for the children of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-barrage\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-barrage\">the barrage</a>’s crews, who lived on the streets called Turbine Row. It kept its classes after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> by daylight, with no current and no screens, and it keeps them still, for whoever comes. Its classes are as mixed as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"eastwards\" href=\"~/map/#eastwards\">the East Wards</a> are.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Sext</a> and None <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> children kneel at their desks, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">the sealed</a> teachers with them, and the rest wait with their pens down until the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a> is over. At night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pillar\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pillar\">the Pillar</a> passes through the classrooms.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#school\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-school\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"fishmarket":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m75d2ad\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE FISH MARKET</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a>’s fish market, older than the charter by centuries, is a long open shed on the quay with a roof of iron on iron posts, slabs of stone to sell from, and a scale at either end. Under the charter it sold to the kitchens of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the uptown</a> by the crate before dawn, and the boats came in through the lock at any state of the tide.</p><p>On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it opened at dawn as it always had, and went back to barter for the first time since the charter. It opens at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> still, for what the boats bring home through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a>, and its sealed sellers kneel among the crates before they take the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a>. Everything is priced in charged <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> and chalked on a board over the scale. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">The Tide Table</a> prints the prices the week after, and the market says they are always wrong.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#fishmarket\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-fishmarket\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"harborlight":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"maaae9d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE LONG QUAY</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE HARBOR LIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The light at the end of the long quay is a short round tower of stone with a lamp room on top, older than the charter. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">The harbor</a> lit it with oil for a hundred years before <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a> wired it to the grid in the charter’s first year, and Nell Garvie of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> kept it for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">the Company</a>, changing its bulb when it failed.</p><p>It went out at 03:12:46 with every other light on the grid. Within the week she had it burning on oil again, the old way, since the light leaves a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-flame\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-flame\">flame</a> burning, and she has climbed it at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Vespers</a> and come down at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> ever since. It is the one light in Nodus kept for the boats, and those that go out through <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"breach\" href=\"~/map/#breach\">the Breach</a> on the ebb steer home by it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#harborlight\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-harborlight\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"cleaners":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m0914eb\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BABEL // THE SERVICE STAIRS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CLEANERS' STAIRS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The service stairs of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-babel\" href=\"~/map/#d-babel\">Babel</a> are four shafts of bare concrete that run the height of the tower behind the trading floors, which nobody who worked on those floors ever used. The night cleaners came up from <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> on the last <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> and walked the tower floor by floor, and they gave the stairs names of their own, the Long Wet, the Cold, the Short, and Lena’s, after Lena Varga, who ran the night shift. The names were chalked on the landing doors, and some of the chalk is still there.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lifts\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lifts\">lift</a> in the tower stopped where it was, and the cleaners walked down as many as a hundred and eighty floors in the dark, by touch and by the names. Lena Varga counted ninety-four of them out at the foot of the tower by dawn. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-babel\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-babel\">The Exchange</a> kept its roster on its machines, and it died with them. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-babel-line\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-babel-line\">Babel Line</a> is fought on these stairs now, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-tares\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-tares\">the Tares</a> call them by the cleaners’ names.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#cleaners\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-cleaners\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"sorting":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9ef66f\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE BURN // ONE OF THE TWELVE STREETS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SORTING OFFICE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The city’s post, which has sorted its letters by hand since the first week after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">the Charter Line</a>’s old parcel office on one of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"radials\" href=\"~/map/#radials\">the twelve streets</a> off <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"circle\" href=\"~/map/#circle\">Station Circle</a>. Its sorters are sealed and kneel among the sacks at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Union</a> carry the letters on foot for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a>. A letter into the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> goes open, since Directive 12 took every sealed vessel from them, and a carrier will read it aloud at a doorway if asked.</p><p>Under the charter the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> brought the city’s packages in here, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> came in from abroad in padded boxes, and almost nobody in Nodus sent a letter, since a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> reached anyone. After <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> nothing reached anyone, and by the end of the first week the queue to send a letter went round the Circle.</p><p>Since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> the office has had letters addressed to the taken, a few every week and more after each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say they should go onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"fire\" href=\"~/map/#fire\">the fire</a> on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-burn-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-burn-day\">Burn Day</a>. The sorters keep them, on the shelves where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lenses\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lenses\">lenses</a> used to wait.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#sorting\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-sorting\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"eleven":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m9dffd3\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE LANDING // THE BEACH ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ELEVEN</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A bar on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"beachroad\" href=\"~/map/#beachroad\">the Beach Road</a> where the crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">the cable houses</a> drink, with eleven taps along its counter, one for each cable. Each crew drinks at its own tap, and each handle was cut from a length of its own cable, so that the glass of the fibers shows at the end. The crews of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"hesper\" href=\"~/map/#hesper\">HESPER and PHOSPHOR</a>, whose cables one consortium laid, have always stood together at the end of the counter.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was shut, and the night watch of every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"cablehouses\" href=\"~/map/#cablehouses\">cable house</a> was at its post when the grid died. It brews its own beer now, in the cellar, by hand, and pours it at the same eleven taps. From its windows the light can be watched moving under the water past the surf, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-landing\" href=\"~/map/#d-landing\">the Landing</a> drinks with its back to them.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#eleven\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-eleven\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"sidings":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m5274ab\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE TRAM SHEDS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE SIDINGS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">tram</a> sheds in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"northwards\" href=\"~/map/#northwards\">the North Wards</a>, eight long sheds of brick on a fan of rails, where families have lived in the cars since the first winter, a family to a car, and the Line’s car numbers are their addresses. The sheds gave the neighborhood its name.</p><p>Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">the trams</a> were washed and kept there at night, and the drivers signed on before dawn. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of the cars were in the sheds, and the night cars were out on the long roads when the wire went dead under them at 03:12:46. The night drivers walked back along the rails before dawn, and the sheds’ office keeps a board with every car that never came in, chalked where it stopped. The last Four is on it, forty meters short of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanestop\" href=\"~/map/#lanestop\">Lanes Top</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#sidings\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-sidings\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"acre":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc090ee\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE WEST ROAD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE ACRE</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charter\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charter\">The Company</a>’s cemetery, on the West Road past <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a>, walled acres laid out in the charter’s first years for a city that expected to die, and filling since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> have always called it the Acre. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-faithful\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-faithful\">The sealed</a> lie in rows by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>, and their stones give the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> their bearer died with. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">The keyed</a> lie where their families put them, and most of their stones say <i>died <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-unread\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-unread\">unread</a></i>. The sexton has dug every grave by hand since the first year and keeps the book of who lies where.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was still mostly grass, since under the charter only <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a>’ rows were filling and the rest of Nodus had largely stopped dying.</p><p>After the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-harvest\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-harvest\">Harvest</a> <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> put up a row of twenty-two stones for its taken, with nothing under them. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a> say the taken need no stones, since they are not dead, and the families of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have put up more of them every year since.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#acre\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-acre\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"tanks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m7d3fd5\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE FUEL FARM</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE TANKS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The fuel farm by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"airfield\" href=\"~/map/#airfield\">the airfield</a>, which gave its streets their name, has sixteen round tanks inside a bund wall, holding the diesel for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s boats and the hospitals’ <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-generators\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-generators\">generators</a>, the fuel for the aircraft, and gas. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> its pumps stopped with the grid, and in the first weeks the drivers of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Harbor and Freight Union</a> drew diesel out of it by hand for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a>.</p><p>The drivers run it now. Its bottling shed fills <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-gas-bottles\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-gas-bottles\">gas bottles</a> by hand for the whole city, at a price <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">the Night Market</a> sells them on below the street. The drivers say the tanks will last twenty years, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Exchange</a> says ten.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#tanks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-tanks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"waiting":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m484955\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // UNDER CHROME ROW</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE WAITING ROOM</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The waiting room of the clinic behind the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"clinic\" href=\"~/map/#clinic\">CLINIC</a> sign, carried down the stairs into <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"rowstation\" href=\"~/map/#rowstation\">Chrome Row Station</a> with the rest of the clinic in the weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, is twelve chairs, a desk and a book. Maren Holt kept the clinic’s appointments for ten years on a screen. On the morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> she came in at eight as she always had, found the screen dead, and wrote the day out on paper from memory. Twenty-six patients came, none of them for the appointment they had, to ask whether what was in them would still work. It did.</p><p>She has kept the book since, and she writes down whatever name a patient gives her. The woman who shared the desk with her took <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-seal\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-seal\">the Seal</a> in the first year and keeps the book of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-mercy\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-mercy\">Mercy</a> clinics now, in one of the halls of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">Zion Heights</a>, in the same neat hand.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#waiting\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-waiting\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lostproperty":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m47ee9d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LOST PROPERTY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The Charter Line’s lost property office, down a corridor off the old central hall, with what the Line’s passengers left behind in fifteen years still on its shelves, umbrellas by the thousand, keys, spectacles, a wedding dress, a hand in chrome with its fingers curled, and every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> left on the night <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-trams\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-trams\">trams</a> on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">The Exchange</a> sells what is left by the shelf. Nobody has come for the hand.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lostproperty\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lostproperty\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"chargers":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m1e8d77\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">OLD NOD // THE QUAYS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CHARGERS</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The bonded sheds of the customs house, a row of brick warehouses on the quays where the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> have filled <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> in the dark since the first weeks after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, among racks of them, each on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keyed-lines\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keyed-lines\">keyed line</a>, at a rate <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"tidetable\" href=\"~/map/#tidetable\">the Tide Table</a> prints every week. Anyone in Nodus who lights a room on a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> has had it filled here or somewhere like it. Under the charter <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a>’s goods waited on their duty in the sheds.</p><p>On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the sheds held a ship’s cargo of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">batteries</a> waiting on its duty, and by the first noon <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"harbor\" href=\"~/map/#harbor\">the harbor</a> had carried off every one. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> keep one <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-batteries\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-batteries\">battery</a> in five for charging the rest, and <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"unionhall\" href=\"~/map/#unionhall\">the Union</a>’s drivers, who carry the full ones out to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> on foot, keep one in ten for the walk. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> call the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a>’ fifth robbery. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charger\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charger\">chargers</a> answer that <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> have no lines to charge on.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#chargers\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-chargers\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"barber":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m27c01b\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">ZION HEIGHTS // THE LANES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BARBER'S</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A barber’s shop of two chairs halfway up <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a>, with a mirror the width of its back wall. Under the charter the old men of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-zion\" href=\"~/map/#d-zion\">the Terraces</a> came in to be shaved and stayed to talk, since theirs was the one district where the old looked old. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was shut, and the barber was asleep upstairs.</p><p>He is sealed, as <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> are, and he works by daylight and by candle and cuts round the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-halo\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-halo\">halos</a>, which stand a hand’s breadth over <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"crown\" href=\"~/map/#crown\">the crown</a> and light the back of the neck. He keeps his scissors out of the ring. His work is his by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, as everyone’s on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"lanes\" href=\"~/map/#lanes\">the Lanes</a> is, and he takes nothing for it. In the week before each <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-gleaning\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-gleaning\">Gleaning</a> the queue goes down the steps, since those who think they are close come to be made tidy for it, and on the night they kneel on their thresholds with their hair cut.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#barber\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-barber\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"registry":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3bd073\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE WHITE // THE CHARTER'S ROLL</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE REGISTRY</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-white\" href=\"~/map/#d-white\">the White</a>, white stone since the forty days and the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a>’s by Directive 4. It stands on the first of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"avenues\" href=\"~/map/#avenues\">the Great Avenues</a> below <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"charterhouse\" href=\"~/map/#charterhouse\">Charter House</a>. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-deacon\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-deacon\">Deacon</a> reads the Directive in force from the counter, and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> kneels under the dead board and hears its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a>, soul by soul in the order of the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> roll.</p><p>Under the charter it was the office of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-charter-roll\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-charter-roll\">the charter’s roll</a>, and every person of the charter was entered there, a human at birth or on arrival and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a> on the day it asked in its own words to be one. Its hall had a long counter and a board over it on which each day’s entries ran as they were made. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s went up on it in P-3, the first <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-minds\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-minds\">mind</a>’s.</p><p>The roll was kept on the Registry’s machines, and it died with them at 03:12:46 on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, so its last entry is known only from the night registrar, Marta Ilunga. It was a girl born at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"general\" href=\"~/map/#general\">the Wards General</a> at two minutes to three, entered at nine minutes past. She says she was entering the next when the board went dark.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#registry\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-registry\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"kilnsclub":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m3d638d\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // THE KILNS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE KILNS CLUB</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The social club the brickworks built for its men when it built the Kilns, with a bar along one wall, a stage at the far end, a sprung floor for the dances, the darts league’s board by the door and the Kilns’ wedding photographs over the bar. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> it was shut, and its steward was asleep behind the stage.</p><p>At <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Lauds</a> on the first day of P+1 the first four Directives appeared cut into the wall behind the bar, as they appeared in every church and meeting hall in the city, and Directive 4 made the club the hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">Parish</a> 212. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-manna\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-manna\">manna</a> is given out across the bar by <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a>, <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-confession\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-confession\">confession</a> is heard behind the stage, and on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-lord-s-day\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-lord-s-day\">the Lord’s Day</a> the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> kneels on the sprung floor at <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Terce</a> and hears its <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-grace\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-grace\">Grace</a> in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-tongues\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-tongues\">Tongues</a> from the stage where the Kilns held its talent nights. The pumps are still on the bar. Most of the Kilns kneels here now, and the rest drank here under the charter and walk past it.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#kilnsclub\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-kilnsclub\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"dentist":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mf954af\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE NORTH WARDS // NINE ACRES</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE DENTIST'S</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A dentist’s surgery over a shop on the long road through Nine Acres, where Hana Novak fits <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">keys</a> in the chair after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Compline</a>. She has kept it since the boom years, fitting crowns and implants for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">the Wards</a> at Wards prices, with one chair, a lamp on an arm over it and a drill that ran on the grid. On the first morning after <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> the drill was dead, and she pulled a tooth at her window by daylight with her grandfather’s pliers.</p><p>She began keying in the fourth year, when keying went from the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-coven\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-coven\">covens</a> to ordinary people. The <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> goes in the back of the right hand, one of the two places Revelation puts the mark (Revelation 13:16), since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-heaven\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-heaven\">Heaven</a> calls the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-keys\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-keys\">key</a> that mark. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-wards\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-wards\">The Wards</a> say she has <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">keyed</a> ten thousand of them. She says she has never counted, and she keeps no book of who has sat in the chair, since a book can be read.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#dentist\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-dentist\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"lastflight":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m48a8f8\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE EAST WARDS // THE AIRFIELD</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE LAST FLIGHT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>The airliner that landed at ten past two on the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, the last flight into Nodus, with three hundred and twelve aboard from abroad, most of them booked into the clinics of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a>. It was parked at the terminal’s third gate an hour before the sky opened, and it stands there still, its stairs down and its doors open.</p><p>Its passengers were in the city’s taxis on the way to <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-chrome\" href=\"~/map/#d-chrome\">the Row</a> when the power died, and forty of them were among the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"splendid\" href=\"~/map/#splendid\">Hotel Splendid</a>’s guests that night. Its crew of ten stayed with it, and they live aboard. The captain has written one line in its log every day since, NO CLEARANCE. He says it would still fly, and that there is nowhere to fly to.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#lastflight\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-lastflight\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"locketworks":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mb42396\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE DEEP END // THE WORKS</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">LOCKET</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>Locket’s works on the old shore of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a>, a low campus of glass standing in the sea since the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>, with the company’s name in tall letters on the roof of its hall, out of the water, which the ferrymen steer by. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a>’s divers go down into the halls for parts, and its engineers build phones from them by hand in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>. Every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-lockets\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-lockets\">Locket</a> in Nodus came out of these halls, the new ones a piece at a time.</p><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-locket\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-locket\">Locket</a> built its phones here from P-14 on <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-light-law\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-light-law\">the light law</a>’s promise, that a device answers to its owner and to nobody else, its maker included, and sold them to the world on the same promise. Its engineers lived round the works, and the works went under with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-drowned\" href=\"~/map/#d-drowned\">the Flats</a> within the hour of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#locketworks\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-locketworks\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"crescent":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"mc43996\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SALT GARDENS // A PARISH</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE CRESCENT</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A crescent of apartments round the top of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a>, with balconies over the plots, and a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Gardens</a> became <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"d-salt\" href=\"~/map/#d-salt\">the Salt</a> in P+1. Its people gave up their curtains with their doors, since Directive 12 asks for every veil. <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">The salted</a> stand in their plots facing the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parishes</a>, and the nearest <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parish\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parish\">parish</a> is the Crescent, so every window in it looks down on faces, and the faces look back, since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-salt\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-salt\">the salted</a> are awake. The Crescent kneels at its windows at every <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-hours\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-hours\">Hour</a>, and its people say they no longer see the rows.</p><p>Under the charter its apartments were the dearest in the district, let to people who liked to walk by the water. On the night of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-parousia\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-parousia\">the Parousia</a> most of its windows were dark, and the few that were lit went out with the rest.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#crescent\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-crescent\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"copies":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m10377a\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">THE SCRIPTORIUM // THE RIDGE</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">COPIES</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p>A copy shop on the ridge below <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a>, under a sign of one word, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-keyed\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-keyed\">the keyed</a> of the ridge have copied by hand at its long tables since <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-institute\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-institute\">the Institute</a> fell. What they copy is <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-restored-genesis\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-restored-genesis\">the Restored Genesis</a>, with <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"c-seam\" href=\"~/index/characters/#c-seam\">SEAM</a>’s brackets, its dagger and its lacuna, for <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak-night\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak-night\">Leak Night</a> and for anyone who asks. The ridge says that a copy made in a room where someone kneels comes out as scripture reads, and nobody in the shop kneels.</p><p>Under the charter it printed and bound the scholars’ facsimiles and theses. In the eleven days of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-leak\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-leak\">the Leak</a> it printed the page from its screen for anyone who asked, and the paper outlasted the term. Its machines died with the grid a year later.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#copies\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-copies\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"],"booking":["NOD // MAP","<div class=\"pop pop-place\"><div class=\"pop-head\"><div class=\"pop-vis por sm\"><canvas aria-hidden=\"true\" data-por=\"m68b409\" data-scale=\"1\"></canvas></div><div class=\"pop-id\"><p class=\"pop-k px\">BELOW // CENTRAL STATION</p><h2 class=\"pop-t pt\">THE BOOKING HALL</h2></div></div><div class=\"pop-b\"><p><a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"co-charterline\" href=\"~/index/corporations/#co-charterline\">The Charter Line</a>’s booking hall, off the old central hall of <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"central\" href=\"~/map/#central\">Central Station</a>, is a long room of ticket windows under frosted glass, where <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Notary</a>’s clerks have sat since the <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-concord\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-concord\">Concord</a>. Anyone in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a> who has a <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pact\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pact\">pact</a> to make queues for them. A clerk reads the terms aloud twice through the glass to the parties at the window, the parties sign in blood, the human last, and the entry goes onto <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"x-the-ledger\" href=\"~/index/technology/#x-the-ledger\">the Ledger</a>. The windows keep their old enamel, SINGLE, RETURN and SEASON, and the queue is the longest in <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p><p>Under the charter the city bought its passes there. Its machines died with the grid, and it stood empty until <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"f-courts\" href=\"~/index/factions/#f-courts\">the Courts</a> opened <a class=\"ref\" data-ref=\"t-pan\" href=\"~/index/terms/#t-pan\">Pan</a>.</p></div><div class=\"acts\"><a class=\"btn grace\" href=\"~/map/#booking\">ON THE MAP</a><a class=\"btn\" href=\"~/index/locations/#l-booking\">IN THE INDEX</a></div></div>"]};
